		REF @DECISION.ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles

DECISION PluginsAreReachedByNameThroughOneResolverAndNeverImported
	TITLE "client, forge, scheduler, collector, check, output and document are plugin kinds"
		+ "resolved by name through one resolver; the core sees documents only and imports no"
		+ "plugin; Clean Architecture's layering is not adopted"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a built-in plugin is a module under its kind's package, an external one an executable"
		+ "brigade-<kind>-<name> on PATH for the client kind; the forge and the scheduler kinds"
		+ "resolve their built-in modules alone until @TASK.B76, post-MVP, delivers their"
		+ "executables; one resolver turns a name into one object answering the kind's operations,"
		+ "searched in the kind's declared order: project, machine, PATH, built-ins; the document"
		+ "kind resolves its two built-in modules, markdown and awawa, which @TASK.B106 delivers"
		REF @TASK.B76
		REF @TASK.B106
	DESC "an operation takes a JSON-compatible dict and returns one, validated by the core on entry"
		+ "as @DECISION.DocumentsCarryAnIntegerSchemaVersionAndAreValidatedOnEntry sets; a module"
		+ "plugin and an executable plugin are indistinguishable to the core; no plugin Python type"
		+ "crosses"
		REF @DECISION.DocumentsCarryAnIntegerSchemaVersionAndAreValidatedOnEntry
	DESC "a client adapter translates: launch answers argv, environment and stdin, result parses"
		+ "the client's output into the normalised document; the core spawns and owns the process"
	DESC "no module outside a plugin package imports a plugin package statically; a plugin is"
		+ "autonomous and imports no other plugin, of its kind or of another; the resolver imports"
		+ "by name at run time; a plugin may import the core and the modules of its kind that"
		+ "answer no operation; the guard of tests/guards parses every module with ast and fails on"
		+ "a static import of brigade.adapters, brigade.collectors, brigade.checks or"
		+ "brigade.outputs from outside their own package, on an import of the package of another"
		+ "kind from a plugin, on an import of a module defining its kind's entry point from"
		+ "another module of that kind, the collect function of a collector included, and on an"
		+ "import of brigade.commands from a plugin, the guard @TASK.B42 asks for, widened"
		REF @TASK.B42
	DESC "cli.py builds the runtime, once per command and once per round of tick --loop through a"
		+ "factory it hands that command: paths, clock, process runner, spawner, resolver; the"
		+ "renderers of a command are declared by its module, as"
		+ "@DECISION.EveryCommandReturnsOneDocumentRenderedOnceAndExitsByOneTable sets; the"
		+ "commands resolve the plugins through the runtime's resolver, and a core function"
		+ "receives resolved plugin objects as arguments and resolves nothing itself, as @TASK.B73"
		+ "delivers; a plugin neither imports nor resolves another plugin: a built-in collector"
		+ "receives the forge resolved by the command in its CollectorEquipment, an executable"
		+ "collector never receiving it"
		REF @DECISION.EveryCommandReturnsOneDocumentRenderedOnceAndExitsByOneTable
		REF @TASK.B73
	DESC "binds @TASK.B06, @TASK.B07, @TASK.B12, @TASK.B14, @TASK.B23, @TASK.B24, @TASK.B42,"
		+ "@TASK.B43, @TASK.B46, @TASK.B47, @TASK.B48 and @TASK.B106"
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B07
		REF @TASK.B12
		REF @TASK.B14
		REF @TASK.B23
		REF @TASK.B24
		REF @TASK.B42
		REF @TASK.B43
		REF @TASK.B46
		REF @TASK.B47
		REF @TASK.B48
		REF @TASK.B106
	REJECTED "a typing.Protocol shared by core and adapters in a common module: an adapter needs no"
		+ "brigade import to answer documents, and the graph stays one-directional"
	REJECTED "calling brigade adapter as a subprocess for a built-in adapter: a process per"
		+ "operation for a module already held; the executable path exists for external adapters"
	REJECTED "Clean Architecture's use case, presenter and ViewModel layering: one delivery"
		+ "mechanism, the command line of DESC 1 of the decision"
		+ "ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles, one persistence, neutral files,"
		+ "adapters already process-shaped, and a port at M3 that carries the contract, not the"
		+ "Python; the rules of the areas architecture and architecture_layers of the instructions"
		+ "corpus govern a core- package, which brigade is not"
	REJECTED "a core function handed a name and the runtime's resolver, the alternative F3 of the"
		+ "foundations review offers: the core would still resolve, and a resolved object passed as"
		+ "an argument is what a unit test replaces with a double"
	REJECTED "a renderer carried by the runtime: no core function renders, the renderers being"
		+ "declared by each command module in its record since pull request #56"
	RATIONALE "it refines DESC 5 and 6 of"
		+ "@DECISION.ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles, DESC 3 of"
		+ "@DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters and plan section 17 to every plugin"
		+ "kind; a shared adapter is created by a factory, never at import, as the rule"
		+ "shared_adapter_created_explicitly of the instructions corpus says"
		REF @DECISION.ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters
	RATIONALE "it departs from the architecture rules of the instructions corpus, the areas"
		+ "architecture and architecture_layers, stated here because this corpus declares no"
		+ "DEROGATES field: those rules govern a core- package, and brigade is a command-line tool"
		+ "with one delivery, one persistence and process-shaped adapters"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 at the refinement of @TASK.B73, amending DESC 5"
		REF @TASK.B73
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-07 at the refinement of @TASK.B76, amending DESC 1: an"
		+ "executable forge or scheduler is post-MVP comfort, F7 of the foundations review"
		REF @TASK.B76
	REJECTED "a unit test of run_segment patching spawn_process in its module: a global module"
		+ "mock, which the rule production_signature_not_deformed_for_test of the instructions"
		+ "corpus refuses; the runtime carries the spawner as it carries the process runner"
	SOURCE "the spawner added to DESC 5 in pull request #65 of the brigade repository, delivering"
		+ "@TASK.B73"
		REF @TASK.B73
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-13 in the refinement of @TASK.B106: the document kind"
		+ "added to the TITLE and to DESC 1"
		REF @TASK.B106
	REJECTED "the fake client importing the markdown and awawa document modules and keeping its own"
		+ "table of them to read the progress: a plugin depending on another plugin, reached"
		+ "outside the resolver"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-14 in the second review round of pull request #122 of the"
		+ "brigade repository, « un plugin doit être autonome et ne pas dépendre d'un autre plugin"
		+ "»: DESC 4 amended"
		REF @TASK.B106
	REJECTED "a built-in collector reaching the forge through a module of brigade/commands/ that"
		+ "resolves it: a plugin depending on another plugin one import away, which the guard of"
		+ "resolver calls does not see"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-18 in the review of pull request #155 of the brigade"
		+ "repository, « Le plugin doit être autonome »: the command passes the forge, a plugin"
		+ "importing brigade.commands is refused by the guard, DESC 4 and 5 amended"
		REF @TASK.B146

DECISION TheTickIsAPurePlannerAndAnExecutorThatRecordsEveryAction
	TITLE "the tick builds one snapshot of the facts, plans its actions as a pure function of that"
		+ "snapshot, and applies them through an executor that records every outcome in the ledger"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a tick builds one snapshot of the facts, ledger-derived states, registry, git facts,"
		+ "forge facts, live processes and now, as frozen dataclasses; the snapshot serialises to"
		+ "one JSON document"
	DESC "plan(snapshot) -> actions is pure: no I/O, no clock, no randomness; an action is a frozen"
		+ "record, launch run, create worktree, merge pull request, pause wave, record event and"
		+ "the like"
	DESC "the executor applies the actions in order through the gateways and plugins handed to it,"
		+ "each action guarded by a fact, an existing branch or worktree reused; it records each"
		+ "outcome in the ledger, a failed action as an event, and goes on with the other actions;"
		+ "the next tick recomputes from facts, so every action is idempotent or guarded by a fact"
	DESC "a tick runs plan and apply rounds until the plan is empty or a cap is reached, so a merge"
		+ "makes its dependents startable in the same tick, as @TASK.B17 asks"
		REF @TASK.B17
	DESC "brigade tick --dry-run prints the snapshot and the plan and applies nothing; a snapshot"
		+ "fixture file is the input of the planner's tests, table-driven on literal rows"
	DESC "due studies and due orders are the same shape: due is a pure function of schedule, last"
		+ "run and now"
	DESC "the tick keeps no truth of its own: the heartbeat of the last tick of @TASK.B28 is a"
		+ "state file written atomically, not a ledger line per empty tick"
		REF @TASK.B28
	DESC "a project whose facts the snapshot cannot read is named on stderr and skipped, and"
		+ "contributes no wave and no milestone to the snapshot, so that the plan, which reads the"
		+ "facts of the project of each wave, serves the other projects"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B07, @TASK.B12, @TASK.B14, @TASK.B17, @TASK.B18, @TASK.B19, @TASK.B48,"
		+ "@TASK.B51 and @TASK.B166"
		REF @TASK.B07
		REF @TASK.B12
		REF @TASK.B14
		REF @TASK.B17
		REF @TASK.B18
		REF @TASK.B19
		REF @TASK.B48
		REF @TASK.B51
		REF @TASK.B166
	REJECTED "an imperative tick with injected gateways: every test needs a fake git, a fake forge"
		+ "and a fake ledger where the planner needs one JSON file"
	REJECTED "a tick state file as the truth: the facts are in the ledger, git, the forge and the"
		+ "corpora, as the decision ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent sets; a state"
		+ "file is derived"
	REJECTED "the fact guards with the stop at the first failure kept: one persistent failure of"
		+ "one project blocks the tick of every project"
	REJECTED "a compensation undoing the effects of a failed action, the worktree and the branch"
		+ "removed on an exception: the decision"
		+ "ThePlanOfAWaveIsWrittenInADetachedWorktreeAndItsBranchCreatedAfterTheCommit already"
		+ "rejects a second write to undo"
	RATIONALE "every transition of @DECISION.ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent is a"
		+ "condition evaluated from facts, and @DECISION.CliDoesTheMechanicalWorkAgentsOnlyJudge"
		+ "leaves no judgement to the tick; the rules test_static_data and test_quality of the"
		+ "instructions corpus want literal rows and time controlled, which a pure planner over a"
		+ "snapshot gives"
		REF @DECISION.ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent
		REF @DECISION.CliDoesTheMechanicalWorkAgentsOnlyJudge
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #9 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-17 in the triage of the use-case map, answer \"Fact guards"
		+ "+ per-action isolation (Recommended)\": DESC 3 rewritten, the stop at the first failure"
		+ "removed, the two alternatives offered added as REJECTED"
	SOURCE "use-case map of 2026-10-16, findings X3, G3 and B10"

DECISION EveryCommandReturnsOneDocumentRenderedOnceAndExitsByOneTable
	TITLE "every command returns one document carrying schema_version, printed as JSON or rendered"
		+ "once as text, and exits by one table of codes mapped in cli.py from the exceptions run"
		+ "raises"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a command module exports one function named after the module, (request, runtime) ->"
		+ "document, a JSON-compatible dict carrying schema_version, or raises, an error or a"
		+ "stand-down, and returns none; --json prints it; the text is rendered from the document,"
		+ "so the text never shows a fact the document lacks"
	DESC "a document is bounded: a long result goes to a file under $XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/ and"
		+ "the document carries its path and a summary; the journal of a run, brigade runs show"
		+ "<id> --log, is bounded record by record and its length is the run's, the reader taking"
		+ "its tail, as"
		+ "@DECISION.ARunKeepsAJournalOfOneShortTimestampedRecordPerActionThatTheReaderTails sets;"
		+ "brigade roles show <slot> returns the resolved role file whole, a text handed whole to a"
		+ "client, and --short bounds it to the front matter and the size of the body, from"
		+ "@TASK.B110"
		REF @DECISION.ARunKeepsAJournalOfOneShortTimestampedRecordPerActionThatTheReaderTails
		REF @TASK.B110
	DESC "stdout carries the document only; stderr carries diagnostics and errors; under --json an"
		+ "error still goes to stderr and stdout stays empty, awawa's convention"
	DESC "exit codes: 0 done, or stood down: another run holds the lock the command needs, one"
		+ "stderr line and stdout empty; 1 the command did not do what was asked, findings, a"
		+ "failed check, a missing prerequisite or a tool failure, with the document when there is"
		+ "one and a stderr line when there is not; 2 usage; 3 refused by policy; 4 paused on"
		+ "quota; 70 brigade's own defect, an unexpected exception with its traceback on stderr,"
		+ "sysexits EX_SOFTWARE"
	DESC "one exception family maps to the table, BrigadeError 1, UsageError 2, PolicyRefusal 3,"
		+ "QuotaPause 4, and StandingDown 0 outside that family, caught in cli.py alone; the"
		+ "message reads brigade <command>: <message>; findings are a document, not an exception"
	DESC "--json and the common options are declared once on a parent parser attached to every"
		+ "subcommand; brigade --version with or without --json stays as @TASK.B01 delivered it"
		REF @TASK.B01
	DESC "a long-lived command, tick --loop, serve or runs show --follow, writes diagnostics to"
		+ "stderr and exits 0 on SIGTERM and SIGINT; brigade keeps no log file of its own besides"
		+ "runs/<id>/; the scheduler adapter decides where stderr goes, the journal or the file the"
		+ "cron line names; the cron line discards the stdout of each tick, its document, which the"
		+ "heartbeat tick.json already records"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B02 first, which introduces the renderer, the exit mapping, the parent parser"
		+ "and the runtime builder, then every command task"
		REF @TASK.B02
	DESC "brigade corpus given -- <awawa args> is the one command that passes another tool's"
		+ "stdout, stderr and exit code through unchanged: its reader is a person at a terminal,"
		+ "brigade's own readers call the gateway; without those args it returns its document, as"
		+ "@TASK.B08 sets"
		REF @TASK.B08
	REJECTED "three codes 0, 1 and 2: the plan's reference already documents 3 and 4 for the wave"
