DECISION ARunKeepsOneDirectoryWithAFolderPerSegmentAndItsResultWrittenLast
	TITLE "a run keeps one directory under runs/<id>/ for all its segments, one folder"
		+ "segments/<n>/ per segment, and result.json written last marks it finished"
	STATUS active
	DESC "runs/<id>/ holds run.json, the record of the run as planned, pid, role.md, progress.md or"
		+ "progress.awawa by the form the document key chooses, journal.jsonl, the journal of the"
		+ "actions of every segment, segments/<n>/ with brief.md, stdout.log, stderr.log and"
		+ "result.json, the run.finished document of that segment, the line the ledger appends, and"
		+ "result.json, that of the last segment"
	DESC "result.json is written atomically after the ledger events of the run: a run with a result"
		+ "is finished, one whose pid lives without it is running, any other is dead"
	DESC "brigade runs stop signals a run only once its process has signalled it is ready: the"
		+ "process runs/<id>/pid names catches SIGTERM, its bit set in the SigCgt mask of"
		+ "/proc/<pid>/status, which brigade run does once its StopSignalReceiver is installed and"
		+ "brigade run --detach never does; a run whose process has not within 10 s is refused, no"
		+ "signal sent"
		REF @TASK.B192
	DESC "a hand-over keeps the run id and numbers the segment; the brief of segment n opens on"
		+ "what the document plugin reads of the progress"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B06, and every task that reads a run, @TASK.B07, @TASK.B19 and @TASK.B106"
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B07
		REF @TASK.B19
		REF @TASK.B106
	REJECTED "a new run id per segment: the ledger's segment field and runs list would split one"
		+ "run into several, and the progress file would move at each hand-over"
	REJECTED "one stdout.log and stderr.log appended across segments: no reader could tell which"
		+ "segment printed a line, and the brief each segment received would be lost"
	REJECTED "a state file rewritten as the run advances: the pid and the result already answer"
		+ "running, finished and dead, without a write a crash could leave half done"
	REJECTED "the outcome of each segment read from the run.finished events of the ledger: brigade"
		+ "runs show would read the monthly ledger files of every run of the machine to find the"
		+ "lines of one, where the directory of the run answers alone"
	REJECTED "a SIGTERM handler installed in brigade/launcher.py before the imports: it changes how"
		+ "every command reacts to SIGTERM"
	REJECTED "a ready file of runs/<id>/ written by the run once its receiver is installed: a"
		+ "second record of the process beside pid, which a stop must match against pid so that the"
		+ "readiness of an earlier process of the run is never taken for its own, where the SigCgt"
		+ "of the process answers alone"
	SOURCE "pull request #24 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B06"
		REF @TASK.B06
	SOURCE "pull request #76 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B79"
		REF @TASK.B79
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-13 in the refinement of @TASK.B106: DESC 1 names the file"
		+ "of each form, DESC 3 what the document plugin reads"
		REF @TASK.B106
	SOURCE "DESC 1 amended in pull request #135 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B151"
		REF @TASK.B151
	SOURCE "DESC 3 and the last two REJECTED added in pull request #166 of the brigade repository,"
		+ "delivering @TASK.B192"
		REF @TASK.B192

DECISION TheCiRunsPinnedDevelopmentToolsThatAreNoDependencyOfBrigade
	TITLE "the CI runs zizmor, ruff, semgrep, vulture, pytest with pytest-xdist and coverage.py,"
		+ "each installed by pip from requirements-ci.txt under dependabot; none is a dependency of"
		+ "brigade, the suite runs in parallel in the test job without coverage, and coverage"
		+ "measures the unit tests alone, in a job of its own, failing below a threshold never"
		+ "lowered"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the CI runs six development tools on every pull request touching a file outside the paths"
		+ "@DECISION.APullRequestTouchingOnlyTheCorpusOrDocumentationRunsNoCodeJob names, and on"
		+ "every push to main: zizmor on .github/workflows/, ruff check and ruff format --check,"
		+ "semgrep scan with the Python and security rule packs, vulture, pytest with pytest-xdist"
		+ "running the suite in parallel on both legs of the test job, without coverage, and"
		+ "coverage.py measuring brigade/ by tests/unit alone in a job of its own on Python 3.11,"
		+ "failing below the fail_under of .coveragerc; @TASK.B62 to @TASK.B66 deliver the first"
		+ "five, one tool per pull request, and @TASK.B190 the parallel run and the coverage of the"
		+ "unit tests alone"
		REF @DECISION.APullRequestTouchingOnlyTheCorpusOrDocumentationRunsNoCodeJob
		REF @TASK.B62
		REF @TASK.B63
		REF @TASK.B64
		REF @TASK.B65
		REF @TASK.B66
		REF @TASK.B190
	DESC "each tool is installed by pip in its CI job from requirements-ci.txt at the repository"
		+ "root, every line pinned to one version; .github/dependabot.yml carries a pip entry for"
		+ "that file next to its github-actions entry, so the pins stay current and covered by"
		+ "dependabot alerts"
	DESC "nothing under brigade/ imports a tool, dist/brigade.pyz ships none and brigade doctor"
		+ "checks none: @DECISION.PythonStandardLibraryOnly binds the program, not the workflow"
		+ "that checks it"
		REF @DECISION.PythonStandardLibraryOnly
	DESC "a tool is configured in the file it resolves from the repository root, ruff.toml,"
		+ ".coveragerc, .github/zizmor.yml; vulture, which reads only pyproject.toml, takes its"
