DECISION ThePidOfARunIsReplacedAtomically
	TITLE "the pid file of a run is replaced atomically, never rewritten in place, so brigade runs"
		+ "list never reads it empty"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every write of runs/<id>/pid, by the foreground process, by brigade run --detach and by"
		+ "the process it re-executes with --run-id, goes through record_run_pid, which writes a"
		+ "temporary file and renames it over pid"
		REF @TASK.B69
	DESC "runs list reports dead a run whose pid file is missing, empty, not of the form <pid>"
		+ "<start time> <boot id>, or naming a process of another identity; an in-place rewrite"
		+ "truncates the file before writing it, and a listing between the two reported a living"
		+ "detached run dead"
		REF @TASK.B136
	REJECTED "runs list reading an empty pid as running: a run that died before writing its pid"
		+ "would then read running forever"
	REJECTED "the process re-executed with --run-id skipping the write of pid: brigade run --run-id"
		+ "without --detach has no earlier process to write it"
	REJECTED "a longer delay of the fake client in the test: the race is in the product, and a"
		+ "slower suite would only hide it"
	REJECTED "the identity of the process in a file of its own beside pid: two writes, where one"
		+ "atomic write keeps the pid and its identity together"
	SOURCE "pull request #45 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B69"
		REF @TASK.B69
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-12 in the refinement of @TASK.B136, delivered by pull"
		+ "request #110 of the brigade repository"
		REF @TASK.B136

