DECISION APullRequestTouchingOnlyTheCorpusOrDocumentationRunsNoCodeJob
	TITLE "a pull request touching only corpus/, docs/, artifact/, wiki/ or Markdown at the root"
		+ "starts no job of ci.yml; a push to main runs them all"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the pull_request trigger of .github/workflows/ci.yml carries paths-ignore corpus/**,"
		+ "docs/**, artifact/**, wiki/** and *.md, the Markdown at the root alone: a pull request"
		+ "changing only those files starts none of its jobs, a pull request changing one other"
		+ "file starts them all"
	DESC "the push trigger on main carries no filter: every merge runs the whole suite"
	DESC "no job of ci.yml reads those paths: the tests write their own corpora in temporary"
		+ "directories, and no .awawa file lies outside corpus/"
	REJECTED "a first job detecting the changed paths and an if: on every job: about fifteen lines"
		+ "of YAML for checks reported skipped, which matter only under required status checks, and"
		+ "main has no branch protection"
	REJECTED "a paths list of the files that start the CI: a file forgotten in the list skips the"
		+ "CI without a warning, where a paths-ignore list starts it for every new kind of file"
	RATIONALE "a pull request of refinement, such as pull request #58 changing corpus/ alone, ran"
		+ "the eight jobs of ci.yml, tests on two Pythons, the floor, zizmor, ruff, semgrep,"
		+ "vulture and coverage, none of which reads a file it changed"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07: paths-ignore of the workflow rather than a detecting"
		+ "job or a paths list, delivered by a pull request of its own without a task"
	SOURCE "DESC 4, the corpus job of @TASK.B95 in a workflow of its own, removed on the user's"
		+ "ruling of 2026-10-10 at the refinement of @TASK.B95: the CI runs no corpus job, by"
		+ "@DECISION.TheTestsThatNeedAwawaReplayRecordedOutputsAndNoTestSkipsInTheCi"
		REF @TASK.B95
		REF @DECISION.TheTestsThatNeedAwawaReplayRecordedOutputsAndNoTestSkipsInTheCi

DECISION ATrailIsWrittenOnlyForWorkDoneAndThePurgeReadsTrailDaysAlone
	TITLE "the trail of a command is written at its end when it ran a subprocess, the trail of a"
		+ "tick once it holds the lock, and the purge of the trails reads trail_days alone"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the records of a command other than run and tick are held until its end, its error path"
		+ "included, and written to commands/<instant>-<command>.jsonl only when it ran a"
		+ "subprocess"
	DESC "the trail of a tick is created once the tick holds the lock, so a tick that stands down"
		+ "writes nothing; tick --dry-run is no tick, and its records go to the trail of its"
		+ "command"
	DESC "the purge parses config.toml itself and reads trail_days alone through read_trail_days:"
		+ "no file means 7 days, a file that is not TOML or a trail_days that is no integer of 1 or"
		+ "more keeps every trail, the other keys are not read"
	DESC "a trail_days that is no integer of 1 or more is an error of read_configuration alone,"
		+ "which brigade doctor reports as a finding naming the key and the file"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B72"
		REF @TASK.B72
	REJECTED "the purge through read_configuration: a config.toml off its shape, client = 1, then"
		+ "fails every command before it runs, brigade doctor included, whose work is to name that"
		+ "defect"
	REJECTED "trail_days the only key allowed to stop every command: a trail_days off its shape"
		+ "then fails every command before it runs, brigade doctor and brigade init included, whose"
		+ "work is to name and repair that defect"
	REJECTED "the trail of a tick located before the lock: a tick that stands down would leave an"
		+ "empty trail where tick --once writes nothing"
	REJECTED "an empty trail for a command that started no subprocess: a file holding no record,"
		+ "nothing for the reader of the trails to read"
	RATIONALE "brigade doctor names a configuration off its shape, so no command may fail on it"
		+ "before doctor runs"
	SOURCE "pull request #60 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-07 on the review of pull request #60, \"option A\": the"
		+ "purge keeps every trail on a trail_days it cannot read, read_configuration keeps"
		+ "reporting the error and doctor names it"

DECISION ForgeAccountsAreBoundPerSlotAndThePolicyChoosesTheReviewMode
	TITLE "config.toml binds a forge login per slot and one for brigade's own gh calls;"
		+ "POLICY.REVIEW chooses approval, verdict or local delivery"
	STATUS active
	DESC "[forge_accounts] of config.toml maps a slot, or the key cli for the gh subprocesses"
		+ "brigade starts itself, to a gh login; a process acting for a bound key carries GH_TOKEN,"
		+ "the token gh auth token --user <login> prints, and an unbound one acts as gh's active"
		+ "account"
	DESC "a bound login whose token gh does not print after forge_attempts attempts stops the"
		+ "command on an error, records the ledger event forge_account.unavailable and pauses the"
		+ "wave; no other account is used in its place; once the preflight exists it checks the"
		+ "logins before a wave"
	DESC "every write to the forge records in its ledger event the login it ran as"
	DESC "POLICY.REVIEW sets the review mode of a project: verdict, the default, the verdict of the"
		+ "review slot recorded in the ledger and the merge into integration needing no GitHub"
		+ "approval; approval, the review slot posting a review that approves or requests changes"
		+ "under its login, distinct from the login of the build slot, and the merge waiting for"
		+ "the approval; local, the tasks merged into integration on the machine and one pull"
		+ "request from integration to main opened once the wave is delivered"
	DESC "a prudence run verifies every task in each mode, as"
		+ "@DECISION.AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate sets; under local it verifies"
		+ "the task branch before its merge on the machine"
		REF @DECISION.AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate
	REJECTED "one forge account for every write, the key forge_account config.toml accepted until"
		+ "now: GitHub refuses an approval by the author of a pull request, so a review slot cannot"
		+ "approve the pull request its build slot opened under the same account"
	REJECTED "forge_account as the default login and [forge_accounts] overriding a slot: the user"
		+ "ruled the table alone, one place naming every login"
	REJECTED "the runs of the client without a token, the pull request opened under the user's"
		+ "active account: the user ruled that the login of the build slot opens it"
	REJECTED "a fallback to gh's active account when a bound login has no token: reviews and merges"
		+ "would run as the user's account, which the branch protection of plan section 18 cannot"
		+ "tell from the bot"
	REJECTED "approval as the default mode: it needs two bot accounts, where verdict runs with one"
	REJECTED "the review mode as a field of PROJECT: how far a project's waves run on their own"
		+ "belongs with AUTO_MERGE in POLICY"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled that brigade adapts to at least three workflows: prudence approving"
		+ "under a bot account distinct from the build account, pull requests merged without"
		+ "approval, and every task delivered on the machine with one pull request once the tasks"
		+ "are delivered; delivered by @TASK.B75, @TASK.B99 and @TASK.B100"
		REF @TASK.B75
		REF @TASK.B99
		REF @TASK.B100
	SOURCE "the user's words of 2026-10-07 at the refinement of B75, \"il faut permettre 2"
		+ "workflow: soit on décide que prudence doit approuver, et dans ce cas on doit lui"
		+ "attacher un compte bot différent du compte de build, soit on décide que les PR seront"
		+ "mergées sans passer par des approvals\"; \"Refuser oui. La vérification de la"
		+ "disponibilité du compte devra se faire en amont (en preflight quand on l'aura"
		+ "implémenté). Si un incident arrive en cours de route, on devra prévoir des attemps pour"
		+ "retry. Et si tout échoue, la run s'arrête avec une erreur critique.\""

DECISION EveryEndOfARunHasItsOwnExitCodeRangedBySeverity
	TITLE "every end of a run has an outcome and an exit code of its own: 0 delivered, 1 to 9"
		+ "errors, 10 to 19 warnings, 20 to 29 normal operation without delivery"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade never infers done: a segment is done only when the run declares it, and every"
		+ "other end, an end the run did not declare included, has its outcome and its code"
	DESC "0 done; 1 failed, an error of the client; 2 a usage error; 3 undeclared, a segment ended"
		+ "without the run's declaration of its end"
	DESC "10 blocked, the run waits for a ruling; 11 wall_limit; 12 turn_limit; 13 soft_limit, a"
		+ "segment its client stopped at the soft limit, @TASK.B114"
		REF @TASK.B114
	DESC "20 handed_over, the run handed over and no hand-over is left; 21 stopped, the run stopped"
		+ "by a signal or by brigade runs stop, @TASK.B109"
		REF @TASK.B109
	DESC "binds @TASK.B102"
		REF @TASK.B102
	REJECTED "a code written only for done, its absence meaning a run still in progress: a run"
		+ "ending on an unknown cause would leave its caller waiting for a done that never comes"
	REJECTED "done at 20 with the other normal codes: the shell, systemd and cron read every code"
		+ "but 0 as a failure"
	REJECTED "one code shared by every end that is not done, or 1 for all of them as B06 does after"
		+ "the last hand-over: a caller such as the tick could not tell a client error from a"
		+ "budget too tight without reading the result"
	RATIONALE "the ranges follow the user's comparison with HTTP status codes, ordered from the"
		+ "most to the least severe; 70, the last resort of brigade/cli.py for an unexpected"
		+ "exception, is left outside them"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 at the drafting of B102, \"toute sortie doit donner"
		+ "lieu à un code\" and \"de 1 à 9 les erreurs, à partir de 10 les warnings et à partir de"
		+ "20 les codes de fonctionnement normal\""

DECISION ARunDeclaresTheEndOfEachSegmentOnTheLastLineOfItsFinalMessage
	TITLE "a run declares how each segment ends on the last line of its final message, and brigade"
		+ "reads that declaration instead of detecting a run still in progress"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the brief announces the line brigade-end: <done|handed_over|blocked>; the adapter reads"
		+ "the last line of the final message the segment's log holds; any other last line is"
		+ "undeclared"
	DESC "a segment ending on undeclared is relaunched on the same count of POLICY.HANDOVERS as a"
		+ "hand-over"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B102"
		REF @TASK.B102
	REJECTED "detecting a hand-over from the progress file, a HANDOVER section or a non-empty file:"
		+ "the file is written after each step and kept at completion, and the section is a"
		+ "convention of the author's instructions, not of brigade"
	REJECTED "a marker line in the progress file: it outlives the segment that wrote it, and"
		+ "brigade would have to strip it before each relaunch"
	REJECTED "a file of its own for the declaration: the adapter would grant a second write beyond"
		+ "the role's capabilities"
	REJECTED "the last brigade-end: line anywhere in the log: a tool output quoting the line would"
		+ "be read as the declaration"
	REJECTED "a count of its own in POLICY for undeclared segments: two bounds on the segments of"
		+ "one run"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07 at the drafting of B102, \"il faut qu'on trouve plutôt"
		+ "un moyen d'enregistrer un marqueur de finition plutôt que d'essayer de détecter si on"
		+ "est toujours en progression\""

DECISION EveryDocumentBrigadeReadsBackAcceptsAnAwawaFormAndTextIsARenderingHandedWhole
	TITLE "every document brigade reads back or parses accepts an awawa form through the plugin"
		+ "kind document; text stays the form of a rendering handed whole to a client, to GitHub or"
		+ "to a person, produced from the entities"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every document brigade reads back or parses, the progress of a run, a role file, a"
		+ "procedure file, a wave report, a study answer and an order output, accepts an awawa form"
		+ "beside its Markdown form, served by the plugin kind document that @TASK.B106 introduces:"
		+ "every operation of the kind takes the document it serves, its path, its schema resource"
		+ "and its frame; a document brigade reads later names its two forms, its schema and its"
		+ "frame when it is specified"
		REF @TASK.B106
	DESC "the awawa form is read entity by entity, status, show and context on the file, never the"
		+ "file whole; the sections a command fills are fields, the narrative a prose field; the"
		+ "schema is shipped by brigade as a resource of its package under a name not ending in"
		+ ".awawa, as @DECISION.ShippedFilesLiveInsideThePackageAndAreReadAsResources sets, and"
		+ "read from no instructions corpus"
		REF @DECISION.ShippedFilesLiveInsideThePackageAndAreReadAsResources
	DESC "a document in its awawa form is validated by awawa lint against that schema, never by a"
		+ "comparison of its headings; a field a command filled is one the answer may not change"
	DESC "a document whose code does not exist yet is designed as entities from the start, its"
		+ "Markdown a rendering for the person and for the dashboard: @TASK.B20, @TASK.B31,"
		+ "@TASK.B48, @TASK.B50 and @TASK.B51 are amended so; the role and the procedure files,"
		+ "whose Markdown form works, gain the awawa form by @TASK.B107"
		REF @TASK.B20
		REF @TASK.B31
		REF @TASK.B48
		REF @TASK.B50
		REF @TASK.B51
		REF @TASK.B107
	DESC "text stays the form of the brief of a segment, segments/<n>/brief.md, of the role file"
		+ "passed to the client, runs/<id>/role.md, and of the file of --brief: a client takes only"
		+ "text, and brigade reads none of the three back"
	DESC "text stays the form of the body of a pull request, of a review reply and of the adapter"
		+ "matrix of the wiki: GitHub and a person read them, brigade parses none"
	DESC "text stays the form of the dated documents of docs/: a dated document is never rewritten,"
		+ "as the rule dated_document_never_rewritten of the instructions corpus sets, and brigade"
		+ "reads none"
	DESC "a text rendering is produced from the entities, as awawa context renders an AGENT entity"
		+ "into the body of a role, and shows no fact its entities lack"
	REJECTED "Markdown kept as the one form of every document, its sections found by headings: a"
		+ "file read whole costs its length at every read, and a comparison of headings validates"
		+ "nothing of the content"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-07 that everything that is a .md must be manageable"
		+ "through awawa instead, and approved the plan of this decision, of @TASK.B107 and of the"
		+ "amendments; the inventory of that day found the brief of a segment, the role file and"
		+ "the file of --brief never read back, brigade/runs/run_segment.py:65-66,"
		+ "brigade/adapters/clients/claude_code.py:65-73 and brigade/runs/plan_run.py:117-123, the"
		+ "progress of a run already served by @TASK.B106, no code of the reports yet, and the"
		+ "triage, the intake and the wave plans already JSONL or entities"
		REF @TASK.B106
		REF @TASK.B107
	RATIONALE "the user wants brigade operational quickly: a form that already works is not"
		+ "rewritten before the MVP, and the comfort of a second form is a task of @MILESTONE.ADD0"
		+ "that brigade may deliver itself; a document whose code does not exist yet costs nothing"
		+ "more as entities"
		REF @MILESTONE.ADD0
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-07: \"d'ailleurs: tout ce qui est un .md doit pouvoir"
		+ "être géré en utilisant awawa à la place, c'est à prévoir dans notre plan\"; on the plan"
		+ "of this decision, of @TASK.B107 and of the amendments: \"ok pour le plan ci-dessus\"; on"
		+ "the priorities: \"J'aimerais avoir une brigade opérationnelle rapidement, et"
		+ "potentiellement les améliorations non indispensables pourront être implémentée en"
		+ "utilisant brigade justement.\""
		REF @TASK.B107

DECISION TheClientIsAskedThroughOneFunctionAndTheConfigurationIsReadOncePerCommand
	TITLE "a client is asked through one function, ask_named_client, which receives the resolved"
		+ "client and the configuration; a command reads config.toml once and passes the record"
		+ "down"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the command modules that ask a client read config.toml once, through read_configuration"
		+ "of brigade/system, whose ConfigurationRequest decides whether a missing file is the"
		+ "default record or a refusal, resolve the client through the runtime's resolver and pass"
		+ "the resolved client and the Configuration record to ask_named_client, which completes"
		+ "the question and resolves nothing"
		REF @TASK.B73
		REF @TASK.B153
	DESC "the ask of a client goes through one function of brigade/system; the configuration"
		+ "travels from the command that read it and the system layer parses no file"
		REF @TASK.B77
	REJECTED "a second ask function, ask_configured_client, reading config.toml itself or kept as"
		+ "an alias of ask_named_client: every command already reads the configuration for the"
		+ "client's name, so it would parse the file twice, and its name no longer guaranteed that"
		+ "the client passed was the configured one"
	RATIONALE "the review of pull request #65 found the double read new in @TASK.B73 and the name"
		+ "dishonest; the draft @TASK.B77 planned to keep the function as an alias, which would"
		+ "have re-introduced it"
		REF @TASK.B73
		REF @TASK.B77
	SOURCE "the review of pull request #65, 2026-10-08, run 20261008T005404Z-e7730d"
		REF @TASK.B73

DECISION ALedgerEventDeclaresEveryFieldBrigadeWritesAndAnUnreportedMeasureIsAbsent
	TITLE "the dataclass of a ledger event declares every field brigade writes and a line must"
		+ "carry them all; a measure no collector reported is absent, never null"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a run.finished line carries the 18 fields describe_finished always writes and a"
		+ "signal.recorded line its 6; the reader refuses a line lacking one, as it refuses any"
		+ "line lacking a field of its event; wall_limit_s is optional on signal.recorded, written"
		+ "on the signal wall_limit_reached alone and absent from every other; steps is optional on"
		+ "signal.recorded, written on the signal budget_exceeded alone"
		REF @TASK.B74
		REF @TASK.B85
		REF @TASK.B103
	DESC "steps_to_first_edit, oversized_output_steps, cost_usd, message and reset are optional on"
		+ "RunFinished: absent from the line until a collector or the client reports them, message"
		+ "also written when the ending brigade decides carries one, and never written null"
		REF @TASK.B83
	DESC "an event the ledger does not declare is read as UndeclaredEvent, its name alone: the"
		+ "overview counts it, and no wave or project view reads a key of its own"
	DESC "the answers of launch-argv and resume-argv share one shape and one kind, ClientCommand"
	REJECTED "keeping the nine fields of EVENT_FIELDS as the read contract of run.finished, the"
		+ "others optional: the dataclass would declare fields a line may lack, and the reader"
		+ "could not tell a damaged line from a complete one"
	REJECTED "writing an unreported measure null: every null of run.finished carries its reason in"
		+ "nulls, and a measure no collector exists for has none to give"
	REJECTED "skipping an undeclared event as an unreadable line: the overview counts the events of"
		+ "every name the ledger holds"
	REJECTED "one dataclass per answer of launch-argv and resume-argv: two identical declarations"
		+ "of one shape"
	REJECTED "one kind for result.json and the parse-result answer: the outcome of result.json"
		+ "admits wall_limit, the cut brigade decides when the wall limit expires, and the client"
		+ "answer never carries it; result.json is the run.finished document of its segment, and"
		+ "the parse-result answer stays a kind of its own"
	SOURCE "pull request #68 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B74"
		REF @TASK.B74
	SOURCE "DESC 1 and DESC 2 amended in pull request #81 of the brigade repository, delivering"
		+ "@TASK.B83"
		REF @TASK.B83
	SOURCE "DESC 1 amended on 2026-10-10 by the user's ruling in the refinement of @TASK.B85"
		REF @TASK.B85
	SOURCE "DESC 1, DESC 2 and REJECTED 5 amended in pull request #135 of the brigade repository,"
		+ "delivering @TASK.B151"
		REF @TASK.B151

DECISION ARunKeepsAJournalOfOneShortTimestampedRecordPerActionThatTheReaderTails
	TITLE "a run keeps a journal, one short timestamped JSON record per action of its client,"
		+ "written as the run goes; brigade prints it whole and the reader takes its tail"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a run appends to runs/<id>/journal.jsonl one JSON record per action of its client,"
		+ "carrying schema_version, the time brigade read it, the segment, the kind and a summary"
		+ "of 200 characters at most, the record naming whether the summary was cut"
	DESC "the journal is written while the segment runs: the run reads the new output of the client"
		+ "every journal_poll_s seconds of config.toml, 2 by default, and once more when the"
		+ "segment ends, so that tail -f of the file follows the run"
	DESC "the actions are read by an operation actions of the client adapter, which turns the new"
		+ "output of a segment into the actions it holds; the core names no event of a client; a"
		+ "client whose adapter declares no such operation has one raw record per line of its"
		+ "stdout, cut to the same length"
	DESC "brigade runs show <id> --log prints the journal, one line per record, and --json the same"
		+ "records in a document; --follow prints it, then each record appended, until the run"
		+ "ends, from @TASK.B113; brigade takes no --tail: the reader pipes the output into tail"
		REF @TASK.B113
	DESC "segments/<n>/stdout.log and stderr.log stay the raw output of the client, the input of"
		+ "its adapter, returned whole by no command"
	DESC "a failure of the journal never ends the segment unbounded: an actions answer the adapter"
		+ "fails to give or brigade refuses journals that output as raw records and the client runs"
		+ "on; any other failure stops the client group before it leaves the wait"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B79"
		REF @TASK.B79
	REJECTED "the paths and line counts of the logs of a segment: the reader opens and searches the"
		+ "files, against DESC 2 of the decision that every trace is read through a brigade command"
	REJECTED "the raw logs returned whole or cut by --tail: the stdout of a vibe segment reached 2"
		+ "MB with a line of 200 655 characters, so a line count bounds nothing"
	REJECTED "a text journal.log followed with tail -f: a brigade reader of the journal would parse"
		+ "a rendering back"
	REJECTED "tail -f of journal.jsonl as the way to follow a run: it prints raw JSON records"
	REJECTED "the segment stopped when its actions operation fails: the journal observes the run,"
		+ "and a client stopped for it loses the work of its segment"
	RATIONALE "the reader of a run, a person or a bot, follows what the run does, not the"
		+ "transcript of its client: vibe writes its whole session on stdout, every turn, its"
		+ "reasoning and the content of every file a tool read, and claude-code under"
		+ "--output-format json writes one result document at the end of the session"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-09 in the refinement of @TASK.B79: \"On ne devrait pas"
		+ "avoir des logs de 2mo. On devrait avoir un journal avec des entrées courtes (1"
		+ "\"ligne\") et horodatées non?\"; \"le tail n'est pas fait à l'intérieur, ça reste à moi"
		+ "(ou au bot) de passer le log en tail\"; on the format, \"en jsonl c'est bien\""
		REF @TASK.B79
	SOURCE "DESC 4 amended and the REJECTED of a --follow of brigade lifted on the user's ruling of"
		+ "2026-10-09 in the refinement of @TASK.B113: \"on a besoin de pouvoir voir défiler le log"
		+ "du run\""
		REF @TASK.B113

DECISION RunFinishedCountsTheMainSessionAndTheSessionWithItsSubAgents
	TITLE "run.finished counts the steps twice: main_steps, the main session, against which a"
		+ "budget and the client's turn limit are read, and total_steps, the session with its"
		+ "sub-agents, the extent of the task"
	STATUS active
	DESC "main_steps replaces steps in run.finished from schema_version 2; a reader of a budget"
		+ "reads main_steps, a reader of the extent of a task reads total_steps"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B83"
		REF @TASK.B83
	REJECTED "the main session alone: steps would not tell the extent of a task that delegates"
	REJECTED "the sub-agents counted into steps: the count would no longer compare with the budget"
		+ "of the procedure nor with --max-turns, which counts the main session alone"
	REJECTED "steps kept and steps_with_subagents or subagent_steps added beside it: the user chose"
		+ "two names that each say what they count, steps being renamed through the upgrade on read"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-09 in the refinement of @TASK.B83: \"steps est aussi"
		+ "utilisée pour connaitre l'ampleur d'une tâche non? On pourrait stocker les 2, il faut"
		+ "juste leur trouver un nom parlant pour qu'on sache que l'un est seulement le main agent,"
		+ "et l'autre est l'agent+subagents\"; the names main_steps and total_steps"
		REF @TASK.B83

DECISION BrigadeCountsStepsAndUsageFromTheTranscriptsAnswerForEveryClient
	TITLE "brigade counts the steps and sums the usage of a session from the transcripts answer,"
		+ "the same way for every client; a client adapter only reads its transcript into that"
		+ "answer"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a message of the transcripts answer carries its id, its usage and the number of its tool"
		+ "calls, and the answer carries the transcript of each sub-agent; the steps of a"
		+ "transcript are its tool calls plus one, its usage the sum over its distinct message ids"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B83 and @TASK.B84"
		REF @TASK.B83
		REF @TASK.B84
	REJECTED "the Claude Code adapter counting, through parse-result called without stdout for a"
		+ "cut segment: each adapter would repeat the counting, and a client whose transcript is"
		+ "read would still need its own rule"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-09 in the refinement of @TASK.B84, \"brigade, de façon"
		+ "générique\""
		REF @TASK.B84

DECISION AKeyAddedToTheClientContractIsRequiredOfEveryAdapter
	TITLE "a key added to an answer of the client adapter contract is required of every adapter,"
		+ "null where the client cannot give it; an adapter that lacks it is refused"
	STATUS active
	DESC "binds @TASK.B83, whose parse-result answer gains cost_usd, and @TASK.B84, whose"
		+ "launch-argv answer gains session_id; an adapter outside the repository, as"
		+ "brigade-client-vibe on PATH, is brought to the contract by its owner when they merge"
		REF @TASK.B83
		REF @TASK.B84
	REJECTED "the new keys optional, an absent one read as null: the contract would no longer say"
		+ "what an adapter answers"
	REJECTED "a schema_version 2 of the answers, version 1 upgraded on read: a weight the user did"
		+ "not want for keys an adapter can answer null"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-09 in the refinement of @TASK.B84, on the session's"
		+ "finding that brigade-client-vibe answers neither key: \"l'adaptateur doit fournir les"
		+ "clés et respecter le contrat non?\""
		REF @TASK.B84

DECISION TheForgeAdapterAnswersTheEnvironmentOfALoginAndDoctorReadsItOnce
	TITLE "the forge adapter answers the environment a process acting as a login carries; brigade"
		+ "doctor reads each bound login once"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the GitHub forge adapter answers read_login_environment with the environment a process"
		+ "acting as a login carries, GH_TOKEN set to the token gh auth token --user prints, or"
		+ "null when gh prints none; brigade adds that environment to the gh subprocesses and"
		+ "client segments of the login and names no variable of gh"
	DESC "brigade doctor reads the environment of each bound login once, with no retry and no"
		+ "ledger event, and reports a login without a token as a warning; forge_attempts and"
		+ "forge_account.unavailable belong to the commands that act as the login"
	DESC "a detached run reads the environment in the command that detaches it, so that a login"
		+ "without a token starts no run, and again in the detached process; the token crosses no"
		+ "argv and no file"
	REJECTED "an answer carrying the bare token, the core naming GH_TOKEN: the variable gh reads"
		+ "would be named outside the adapter of gh"
	REJECTED "doctor reading each login through forge_attempts: the report would wait seconds per"
		+ "login without a token and stop on the error its forge items report as a warning"
	REJECTED "the token handed to the detached process in its environment: the runner adds nothing"
		+ "to the environment of brigade itself, and a second read costs one gh call"
	SOURCE "pull request #80 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B75"
		REF @TASK.B75

DECISION TheSessionOfASegmentIsTheOneItsResultReportsElseTheOneNamedAtLaunch
	TITLE "the session of a segment that exits is the one its parse-result answer reports, the"
		+ "session named at launch when it reports none; a segment cut at the wall-time limit takes"
		+ "the session named at launch"
	STATUS active
	DESC "binds @TASK.B84"
		REF @TASK.B84
	REJECTED "the session named at launch for every segment: the fake answers unchanged the session"
		+ "brigade generates, so the transcripts recorded for fake-session in tests/cli/test_run.py"
		+ "would no longer be read, against the SPEC of the task that keeps those rows passing, and"
		+ "a client naming its session in its result only would lose it"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-09 on the review of pull request #86 of the brigade"
		+ "repository, the coded session kept and SPEC 1 of @TASK.B84 rewritten to state it:"
		+ "\"ok\", answering \"On garde le comportement codé et on réécrit SPEC 1 ?\""
		REF @TASK.B84

DECISION ALedgerViewCountsARunOnceByItsLastSegmentAndSumsTheStepsOfItsMeasuredSegments
	TITLE "a view of brigade ledger counts a run once, by the outcome of its last segment, and"
		+ "measures it by the sum of its measured segments, marked partial when one is not measured"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a view of brigade ledger that counts or measures runs groups the run.finished events by"
		+ "run id; the outcome and the error class of a run are those of its last event, and the"
		+ "overview counts the segments, by outcome and by error class, beside the runs"
	DESC "the steps of a run are the sum of the main_steps of its measured segments; a run whose"
		+ "sum lacks a segment is partial, counted as such in every summary of steps and kept in"
		+ "its percentiles, so that a computation can leave it out"
	DESC "every summary of steps gives the runs and the segments side by side, the segments being"
		+ "what the budget of a procedure caps; a run is dated by its last run.finished event"
	DESC "the runs measured are those with a sum, the partial runs among them, so that the partial"
		+ "runs are a part of the measured runs and the unmeasured runs are those with no measured"
		+ "segment"
	DESC "the steps to the first edit of a run are partial only when a segment before the first one"
		+ "reporting steps_to_first_edit lacks its main_steps: the segments after the first edit,"
		+ "measured or not, leave the value exact, so that partial marks an underestimate alone"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B86 and every later view of the ledger, @TASK.B37 among them"
		REF @TASK.B86
		REF @TASK.B37
	REJECTED "one count per run.finished event: a run cut and resumed counts once per segment, and"
		+ "a segment cut on the step cap stops at the budget, so the budget measures itself"
	REJECTED "a run with an unmeasured segment left unmeasured: the steps its measured segments"
		+ "spent would be lost to every summary"
	REJECTED "the sum of the measured segments with nothing marking it: an underestimate could not"
		+ "be told from a measure and left out"
	REJECTED "the error classes counted by run alone: the turn limits that ended intermediate"
		+ "segments would vanish from the overview"
	REJECTED "the steps summarised by run alone: the steps a segment takes, which the budget caps,"
		+ "would vanish from every view"
	REJECTED "a run dated by its first segment: a run would enter a period of ledger compare before"
		+ "it is finished"
	REJECTED "the partial runs counted apart from the measured runs: measured would no longer count"
		+ "the runs that enter the percentiles, as it does for the segments"
	REJECTED "the steps to the first edit partial when any segment of the run lacks them: every run"
		+ "whose first edit falls in a later segment would be marked partial while exact, and left"
		+ "out with the underestimates"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-10 in the refinement of @TASK.B86"
		REF @TASK.B86
	SOURCE "pull request #91 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B86: the runs measured"
		+ "include the partial runs"
		REF @TASK.B86
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-10 on the review of pull request #91, \"Sous-estimation"
		+ "seule\": the steps to the first edit are partial only when a segment before the first"
		+ "edit has no main_steps measured"
		REF @TASK.B86

DECISION TheStepCapOfClaudeCodeBoundsAnswersAndTheBudgetIsWatchedInSteps
	TITLE "the --max-turns brigade passes to Claude Code caps the model's answers, not brigade's"
		+ "steps; its computation stays the budget plus a quarter, and a segment over its budget in"
		+ "steps is caught by the signal budget_exceeded"
	STATUS active
	DESC "Claude Code's --max-turns counts the answers of the model; its num_turns, like the steps"
		+ "brigade counts, is one plus the tool results, so an answer carrying several tool calls"
		+ "adds several steps and a single turn"
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeCountsStepsAndUsageFromTheTranscriptsAnswerForEveryClient
	DESC "binds @TASK.B103"
		REF @TASK.B103
	REJECTED "a --max-turns computed so that the steps hold under the budget: no value bounds the"
		+ "steps, an answer carrying any number of tool calls"
	REJECTED "reading num_turns as a count of answers, to blame the client for a cap not applied:"
		+ "session eca43c28 made 12 answers under --max-turns 50"
	RATIONALE "session eca43c28 of run 20261007T175404Z-6108de holds 12 distinct assistant message"
		+ "ids, 56 tool calls and num_turns 57; Claude Code 2.1.296 under --max-turns 2 made 2"
		+ "answers carrying 3 parallel tool calls and ended success with num_turns 4"
	SOURCE "pull request #104, delivering @TASK.B103"
		REF @TASK.B103

DECISION AProjectChoosesHowBrigadeUsesItsCorpus
	TITLE "a project whose repository already holds a corpus chooses how brigade uses it: brigade"
		+ "controls it, keeps to an area of it, or works without awawa; the mode is a field of the"
		+ "PROJECT entity and control is delivered first"
	STATUS active
	CLOSES @OPEN_QUESTION.HowBrigadeJoinsAProjectWhoseCorpusAlreadyExists
	DESC "control: brigade writes its MILESTONE and TASK entities in the project's corpus and"
		+ "refuses, naming them, the types and fields its schema does not declare"
	DESC "area: brigade keeps to an area of its own in the repository; none: the project's waves"
		+ "and tasks do not go through awawa, brigade itself still requiring it"
	DESC "brigade project add, finding a corpus in the repository, asks the user which mode to set;"
		+ "a project without a corpus is in control, brigade creating its corpus"
	DESC "the mode is a field of the PROJECT entity of projects.awawa, beside CORPUS"
	DESC "control is delivered first, by @TASK.B10 and @TASK.B139; area and none by @TASK.B140"
		REF @TASK.B10
		REF @TASK.B139
		REF @TASK.B140
	REJECTED "a single answer for every project, shared or separate: the user wants the choice"
	REJECTED "the mode in config.toml: the PROJECT entity already holds the corpus folder of the"
		+ "project"
	REJECTED "the three modes delivered together by the first planning task: the none mode is not"
		+ "designed yet"
	RATIONALE "awawa stays a prerequisite of brigade, by"
		+ "@DECISION.BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites; the none mode concerns a"
		+ "project's waves and tasks, not brigade's own corpus"
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-12 in the refinement of B10: \"si on détecte un corpus"
		+ "préexistant, on doit poser la question à l'utilisateur: soit il veut que brigade"
		+ "contrôle le corpus, soit il veut que brigade se confine dans une aire, soit il ne veut"
		+ "pas que brigade passer par awawa. Le tout rendu configurable dans le fichier de config\""

DECISION ThePlannerWritesEveryOverlapRulingAsAnAfterEdge
	TITLE "two tasks of a wave that touch the same files are ordered by an AFTER edge the planner"
		+ "writes, and the tick reads no other order"
	STATUS active
	DESC "when the planner finds that two tasks of a wave touch the same files, it writes AFTER on"
		+ "the one that goes second, naming the first"
	DESC "the scheduler orders tasks by their AFTER edges alone"
		REF @TASK.B12
	REJECTED "a field of SCHEMA WAVE listing the overlapping pairs, launched apart with no merge"
		+ "order: the second task still has to start from a base holding the first to avoid a"
		+ "conflict, which an AFTER edge already gives"
	RATIONALE "the Blueprint, plan section 5, rows 2 and 4, has the planner rule the overlaps and"
		+ "the tick take its order from the plan; one mechanism the tick already reads keeps the"
		+ "schema of a wave free of a second ordering"
		REF @TASK.B10
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-12 in the refinement of B12"
		REF @TASK.B12

DECISION TaskPullRequestTitleIsTheTypeComponentAndAShortImperativeSubject
	TITLE "the pull request of a task is titled TYPE(COMPONENT): <subject> (@TASK.<task>), TYPE a"
		+ "required field of the task and the subject short, opening on a verb in the imperative"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a task brigade delivers carries TYPE, a Conventional Commits type, and brigade task pr"
		+ "refuses a task without one"
	DESC "the title is TYPE(COMPONENT): <subject> (@TASK.<task>), the scope left out when the task"
		+ "has no COMPONENT"
	DESC "the scope is the COMPONENT with its spaces replaced by hyphens: the pass is written"
		+ "the-pass"
	DESC "the subject is short and opens on a verb in the imperative; the author of the pull"
		+ "request writes it, from no field of the task"
	REJECTED "the TITLE of the task as the subject, the form ruled on 2026-10-12: a TITLE is a noun"
		+ "phrase stating the task whole, so the title opened on no verb and ran the length of the"
		+ "task"
	REJECTED "the subject of the first commit of the branch, with or without TYPE as a fallback:"
		+ "the user ruled that the task carries the type"
	REJECTED "the type as the prefix of the task id, the convention of the instructions corpus:"
		+ "every brigade task would be renamed and a project of untyped ids could deliver nothing"
	REJECTED "a type derived from the task, feat by default: often wrong"
	RATIONALE "the branch task/<slug>/<task> names no type, and the rule"
		+ "conventional_commit_subject of the instructions corpus binds the title of a pull request"
		REF @TASK.B12
	RATIONALE "that rule checks the form type(scope): subject only, no subject length and no mood:"
		+ "the length and the mood of the subject are brigade's own ruling"
	RATIONALE "the commit-msg hook of the instructions corpus accepts a scope matching"
		+ "[a-zA-Z0-9._/-]+ only, so a COMPONENT holding a space cannot be the scope as it is"
		+ "written"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-12 in the refinement of @TASK.B142"
		REF @TASK.B142
	SOURCE "the user's words of 2026-10-15 on PR #134, titled from the TITLE of @TASK.B60: « le nom"
		+ "de la pr 134 est trop long et ne commence pas par un verbe à l'impératif »; the"
		+ "amendment chosen: « le titre d'une PR de tâche est type(scope): un verbe à l'impératif,"
		+ "court, puis (@TASK.X) »"
		REF @TASK.B60
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-15 on the question of the review of #141, whether the-pass"
		+ "is the written form of the COMPONENT the pass in a title: « Espaces en tirets — La"
		+ "portée est le COMPONENT, ses espaces remplacés par des tirets. »"
		REF @TASK.B99

DECISION AWaveIsAMilestoneOfTheProjectCorpusAndItsBranchIsNamedAfterIt
	TITLE "a wave is a MILESTONE of the project's corpus, its plan one MILESTONE entity and its"
		+ "TASK entities; the REQUEST names it in MILESTONE, and its integration branch is"
		+ "integration/<NAME>-<TITLE as a slug>"
	STATUS archived
	DESC "replaced by @DECISION.AWaveIsABatchOfTasksStartedTogetherAndLivesInTheLedgerAlone on the"
		+ "user's rulings of 2026-10-17: a wave is a batch of tasks recorded in the ledger, a"
		+ "MILESTONE a goal grouping, and the integration branch is integration/<project>_w<n>"
		REF @DECISION.AWaveIsABatchOfTasksStartedTogetherAndLivesInTheLedgerAlone
	DESC "the plan of a wave is one MILESTONE entity and the TASK entities whose MILESTONE names"
		+ "it, written in the project's corpus; brigade declares no WAVE type"
	DESC "SCHEMA REQUEST of the shipped operational schema carries MILESTONE, the name of that"
		+ "entity, in place of WAVE"
	DESC "the integration branch of a wave is integration/<NAME>-<slug>, NAME the name of the"
		+ "MILESTONE and slug its TITLE lowercased with every run of characters other than letters"
		+ "and digits replaced by one hyphen, integration/M9-runs-list-as-json for M9 \"runs list"
		+ "as JSON\"; a branch already existing at that name is a refusal of brigade plan record"
		+ "naming it"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B139, @TASK.B10, @TASK.B11, @TASK.B12, @TASK.B13 and @TASK.B55"
		REF @TASK.B139
		REF @TASK.B10
		REF @TASK.B11
		REF @TASK.B12
		REF @TASK.B13
		REF @TASK.B55
	REJECTED "a WAVE type distinct from MILESTONE: for the user a wave and a milestone are one"
		+ "thing, and brigade's own corpus groups its tasks by MILESTONE, TASK.MILESTONE being"
		+ "required"
	REJECTED "integration/<slug> cut from the text of the request or from its number alone: the"
		+ "branch names the wave, and the user chose the name and the title of its milestone"
	RATIONALE "the user's words: « si c'est une branche d'intégration, ça devrait être le nom de la"
		+ "wave (ou milestone, pour moi wave=milestone) » and « Oui MILESTONE mais REQUEST.WAVE"
		+ "doit être renommé REQUEST.MILESTONE je suppose »; no SCHEMA WAVE existed anywhere, and"
		+ "brigade/corpus/data/schema.awawa.tpl:126 declared FIELD WAVE string on REQUEST"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-13 in the refinement of B139, B44 and B47"

DECISION ASlotClientIsBoundByTheSlotClientsTableOfConfigToml
	TITLE "the table [slot_clients] of config.toml binds a slot to a client adapter; a run's client"
		+ "is the slot's, else PROJECT.CLIENT, else the client key"
	STATUS active
	DESC "[slot_clients] maps a slot among the nine to the name of a client adapter, in the shape"
		+ "of [forge_accounts]; an unknown slot or a value that is no string is an error naming the"
		+ "key and the file"
	DESC "the client of a run is the one [slot_clients] binds to its slot, else the CLIENT of the"
		+ "PROJECT entity, else the client key of config.toml"
	DESC "the client is a property of the machine: a role file and an AGENT entity name no client,"
		+ "and a role stays portable between machines"
	DESC "brigade roles list probes the client of each slot [slot_clients] binds to another client,"
		+ "once per client, and shows the model it binds; an adapter found nowhere exits 1, as one"
		+ "the client key names does"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B145; it stands beside DESC 1 of"
		+ "@DECISION.ASlotIsBoundByTheSlotsTableOrByTheSlotItsRoleFileDeclares, [slots] binding the"
		+ "role and [slot_clients] the client"
		REF @TASK.B145
		REF @DECISION.ASlotIsBoundByTheSlotsTableOrByTheSlotItsRoleFileDeclares
	REJECTED "a client key inside [slots]: a row of [slots] is one string, the name of an AGENT"
		+ "entity, and [forge_accounts] already shows the form of a per-slot binding, a table of"
		+ "its own"
	REJECTED "a client field of the role file: the client is a property of the machine, and a role"
		+ "file naming one would no longer be portable"
	REJECTED "an empty model cell in brigade roles list for a slot bound to another client: the"
		+ "column states the model the role runs on, and a slot bound elsewhere is where it is most"
		+ "useful; the client of the slot is probed instead"
	RATIONALE "the user's words: « config.toml : [slot_clients] review = \"vibe\" ; ordre : slot,"
		+ "sinon PROJECT.CLIENT, sinon client ; même forme que [forge_accounts]. Le client est une"
		+ "propriété de la machine, le rôle reste portable. »; the question is the user's of"
		+ "2026-10-07, recorded in @TASK.B44, whether two AI providers can coexist"
		REF @TASK.B44
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-13 in the refinement of B139, B44 and B47"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-15 on the review of pull request #140: « Probe du client"
		+ "du slot (Recommandé) — Un probe par client distinct de [slot_clients]. La colonne garde"
		+ "son sens (le modèle sur lequel tourne le rôle) là où c'est justement le plus utile. Le"
		+ "run décide quoi faire si ce client n'est pas installé et le prouve par un test. »"

DECISION BrigadeRunsAwawaOnAProjectFromThePathItsAnchorsResolveFrom
	TITLE "brigade reads a project's corpus with the project's PATH as the awawa workspace, the"
		+ "root its anchors resolve from; a project whose PROJECT entity has no CORPUS has no"
		+ "corpus to plan from"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every awawa command brigade runs on a project's corpus names PATH as the workspace and"
		+ "runs there; CORPUS tells whether the project has a corpus, and awawa finds its files"
		+ "under PATH"
	DESC "brigade plan record names the root of its detached worktree of PROJECT.MAIN, the same"
		+ "repository root at the commit the plan is written on, for every check of the plan and"
		+ "for the write"
		REF @DECISION.APlanReusingANameOfTheCorpusIsRefusedBeforeAnyWrite
	DESC "brigade plan context on the request of a project with no CORPUS exits 1 naming the"
		+ "project, until brigade project add --init-corpus of @TASK.B55 gives such a project its"
		+ "corpus"
		REF @TASK.B10
		REF @TASK.B55
	REJECTED "PATH joined to CORPUS as the workspace: the anchors of this repository resolve from"
		+ "its root, not from corpus/, and a narrower workspace reports every anchor broken (L016)"
	RATIONALE "awawa walks the workspace it is given and skips what git ignores, so PATH reads the"
		+ "corpus alone, worktrees under .claude/ included; the help of awawa asks for the root the"
		+ "anchors resolve from, never a narrower directory"
	SOURCE "pull request #117 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B10"
		REF @TASK.B10
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-13 on pull request #117: the decision is ratified, with"
		+ "the reference to @TASK.B55"
		REF @TASK.B55

