		REF @DECISION.EveryEndOfARunHasItsOwnExitCodeRangedBySeverity
	REJECTED "adding brigade-end: failed to the outcomes a run declares: it would change the"
		+ "decision on how a run declares the end of each segment and the client adapter, and"
		+ "failed would no longer mean an error of the client only"
	REJECTED "dropping the check because brigade plan record lints the corpus: the one correction"
		+ "round of plan record would be spent on errors the planner finds without writing"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-13 on pull request #117 of the brigade repository, « je"
		+ "suis d'accord avec tes recommendations, go », on « garder 3.2 comme pré-vérification"
		+ "sans écriture, mais en failed »"
