DECISION APlanReusingANameOfTheCorpusIsRefusedBeforeAnyWrite
	TITLE "a plan entity whose name the project's corpus already holds is refused before any write"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade plan record reads awawa status of the corpus PROJECT.MAIN holds, in the detached"
		+ "worktree the plan is written in, before any other check of the plan and exits 1 naming"
		+ "each entity of the plan whose type and name the corpus already holds, with the file and"
		+ "the line where it sits: @TASK.S2 already exists at corpus/tasks.awawa:812; nothing is"
		+ "written"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B139"
		REF @TASK.B139
	REJECTED "leaving the collision to the lint round: awawa new exits 1 on the name before lint"
		+ "runs, so the planner reads that the schema does not declare the type, and a collision"
		+ "lint caught would spend the one lint round of the run on a mistake a read finds before"
		+ "any write"
	REJECTED "reading the checkout at PROJECT.PATH: a checkout on a branch behind PROJECT.MAIN"
		+ "misses a name PROJECT.MAIN holds, and the write fails awawa lint --strict on a duplicate"
		+ "identity, spending the one lint round of the run; the check of the schema reads the same"
		+ "corpus for the same reason"
	SOURCE "pull request #121 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B139"
		REF @TASK.B139
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-14 on pull request #121 of the brigade repository, «"
		+ "option A pour le finding 1 (refuser la collision avant toute écriture), ok pour ta"
		+ "variante de l'option 2 pour le finding 7 »"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-14 on pull request #121 of the brigade repository, « 2:A"
		+ "», on « lire le corpus de PROJECT.MAIN, là où le plan s'écrit : les collisions sont"
		+ "toujours vues avant écriture ; list_undeclared, qui a le même défaut, est aligné »"

DECISION ATestDoubleIsNamedAfterTheSubjectItImitates
	TITLE "a test double of the suite is named <Subject>Double, after the subject it imitates, and"
		+ "need not carry an agent noun"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a double imitating a whole plugin, a port or a client is named after that subject, as"
		+ "ClientDouble, ForgeDouble, AwawaDouble and DocumentPluginDouble are; a double answering"
		+ "one behaviour of its subject may still say it, as ClientRefusingToReadTranscriptsDouble"
		+ "or EntryDetectorDouble do"
	REJECTED "an agent noun for every double, as the rule class_named_after_its_work of the"
		+ "instructions corpus asks, DocumentOperationsAnswererDouble for DocumentPluginDouble: a"
		+ "double imitates its subject, so the name of the subject already says the work it does"
	RATIONALE "it departs from the rule class_named_after_its_work of the instructions corpus,"
		+ "which asks a test double of a service or an adapter for an agent noun and lets no"
		+ "category word replace it; stated here because this corpus declares no DEROGATES field: a"
		+ "double imitates its subject, so the subject's name already says what it does, and the"
		+ "suite holds doubles of this shape since its first runs, ClientDouble in"
		+ "tests/unit/runs/test_run_segment.py and the three ForgeDouble of tests/unit/system"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-14 on the third review round of pull request #122 of the"
		+ "brigade repository, « 1:A », option A: « <Sujet>Double accepté pour les doublures : une"
		+ "DECISION du projet déroge à class_named_after_its_work en la nommant, avec la raison »"
		REF @TASK.B106

DECISION EveryLaunchOfASubprocessOfTheTestsGoesThroughTheProcessLauncher
	TITLE "every subprocess of tests/ is launched by tests/process_launcher.py, whose two calls are"
		+ "the only S603 exemptions of tests/, and a guard refuses a launch anywhere else"
	STATUS active
	DESC "ProcessLauncher.run and ProcessLauncher.start of tests/process_launcher.py hold the only"
		+ "calls of subprocess.run and subprocess.Popen of tests/, each with one noqa S603"
		+ "commented with its cause; argv, cwd, environment, input and limits come from the caller,"
		+ "and run takes check as a required keyword"
	DESC "tests/guards/find_subprocess_launches.py refuses a call of subprocess.run or"
		+ "subprocess.Popen, through an aliased import too, and a from subprocess import of either,"
		+ "anywhere in tests/ but that module; the constants, exceptions and types of subprocess"
		+ "stay free to read"
	DESC "the guard is the check of SPEC 1 of @TASK.B152: its spec quotes the call as text in its"
		+ "rows, as tests/guards/test_subprocess_uses.py does, so the grep of that SPEC names both"
		+ "beside the launcher"
		REF @TASK.B152
	DESC "the unused-noqa check of tests/ is ruff check --extend-select RUF100 tests: --select"
		+ "RUF100 alone enables no other rule and reports every exemption, the two S603 and the"
		+ "DTZ001 of tests/unit, as unused and non-enabled"
	REJECTED "brigade/system/run_process.py as the launcher of the tests: it is the code under"
		+ "test, and its whitelisted environment and its ToolFailure would stand between a test and"
		+ "the fake awawa or the hook command it launches"
	RATIONALE "S603 and S607 do not hold the convention alone: S603 spares an argv of literals and"
		+ "S607 an argv whose first literal is an absolute path, as the two launches of"
		+ "tests/cli/test_zipapp.py with no exemption showed on ed63f4a; a guard holds it, rule"
		+ "repository_rule_has_a_guard of the instructions corpus"
	SOURCE "pull request #127 of the brigade repository, which delivers @TASK.B152 on 2026-10-14"
		REF @TASK.B152

DECISION TheRuffFamiliesBrigadeSelectsAndTheOnesItRefuses
	TITLE "ruff.toml selects, beside S, B, UP and C901, the 17 families the code already satisfies"
		+ "and DTZ, SIM, PERF, RUF, ERA and T20, then PTH and FBT once their tasks land; N, E501,"
