DECISION APullRequestOfBrigadesOwnWaveIsReviewedAndItsReviewAnsweredByBrigadeRuns
	TITLE "a pull request of a wave of brigade's own tasks is reviewed by a brigade run of the"
		+ "review slot, and the findings of that review are addressed or challenged by a brigade"
		+ "run awawa-pr-review-round"
	STATUS archived
	DESC "archived on the user's ruling of 2026-10-24: from M2 brigade delivers its own milestones"
		+ "through its tick, as it does for any registered project, and its pull requests fall"
		+ "under @DECISION.AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate, the preflight then one"
		+ "prudence run before the merge into integration/<wave> and the user merging the"
		+ "integration pull request into main, with the candidates of a wave as"
		+ "@DECISION.AWaveIsABatchOfTasksStartedTogetherAndLivesInTheLedgerAlone sets since that"
		+ "day"
		REF @DECISION.AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate
		REF @DECISION.AWaveIsABatchOfTasksStartedTogetherAndLivesInTheLedgerAlone
	DESC "every pull request of a wave of brigade's own tasks, the waves of the Bootstrap section"
		+ "of AGENTS.md, is reviewed by a brigade run of the slot review, pr=<n> its argument,"
		+ "which posts one COMMENT review with one inline comment per finding"
	DESC "a review that leaves findings is answered by a brigade run awawa-pr-review-round --slot"
		+ "build pr=<n>, which addresses or challenges every thread"
	DESC "neither the review nor the answer to it is done by the session itself or by an Agent call"
	REJECTED "the session reviewing the pull request, or answering its threads, itself or through"
		+ "an Agent call: the user ruled that both are brigade runs"
	REJECTED "the ruling extended to every project, as a POLICY or as a rule of the instructions"
		+ "corpus: asked whether it holds for this project or for every project, the user answered"
		+ "« projet »"
	RATIONALE "@DECISION.AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate and"
		+ "@DECISION.ForgeAccountsAreBoundPerSlotAndThePolicyChoosesTheReviewMode rule the waves"
		+ "brigade runs for its users, on an integration branch under POLICY.REVIEW; brigade's own"
		+ "waves run today as one pull request per task on main, launched by hand from the"
		+ "Bootstrap section, and this decision carries the same principle, delivered work never"
		+ "verified by the run that produced it, to those pull requests"
		REF @DECISION.AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate
		REF @DECISION.ForgeAccountsAreBoundPerSlotAndThePolicyChoosesTheReviewMode
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-15, during the wave M1 launched by /awawa-plan-wave-start:"
		+ "« chaque pr devra être relue par une revue via brigade, puis s'il y a des feedbacks, ils"
		+ "devront être traités ou challengés via un run brigade également »; asked whether it"
		+ "holds for this project or for every project: « projet »"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-24 on pull request #201 of the brigade repository, which"
		+ "rewrites the Bootstrap section of AGENTS.md: « Brigade livre en effet des Milestone"
		+ "complètes, pas besoin d'une décision normalement c'est censé être le cas prévu. »; « Ah"
		+ "ok donc la décision doit être archivée ou amendée »; « Archiver (Recommended) — STATUS"
		+ "archived, avec une DESC qui renvoie à AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate et à"
		+ "ta décision d'aujourd'hui. »; archived in pull request #202"

DECISION CollectWithoutSinceCollectsFromTheBeginning
	TITLE "brigade collect without --since hands its collector BRIGADE_SINCE 1970-01-01: the"
		+ "collection runs from the beginning"
	STATUS active
	DESC "--since <n>d or <date> narrows a collection; without it BRIGADE_SINCE is 1970-01-01, a"
		+ "date as the contract of @TASK.B47 requires, and the cache keys that date like any other"
		REF @TASK.B47
	REJECTED "a default window such as 7d: a default counted from the clock keys a new cache entry"
		+ "every day and cuts history a caller never asked to cut"
	REJECTED "an empty BRIGADE_SINCE: the contract names a date, and every collector would have to"
		+ "tell the empty value apart"
	RATIONALE "the task left the default open, writing --since between brackets; the beginning is"
		+ "the one default that drops nothing and is the same on every day"
	SOURCE "pull request #136 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B47"
		REF @TASK.B47
	SOURCE "the user's ratification of 2026-10-15 on review 5525912035 of pull request #136 of the"
		+ "brigade repository: « Ratifier telle quelle (Recommandé) — Sans --since, la collecte"
		+ "part du début, comme brigade ledger : une seule convention dans l'outil. La décision"
		+ "reçoit votre ratification comme source. »"

DECISION ACollectorDeclaresInItsDocumentWhetherItIsCached
	TITLE "a collector declares that its document is cached by the key cache, true, of the document"
		+ "it prints; a collector that declares nothing is never cached"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the document a collector prints may carry cache, a boolean validated with the rest of its"
		+ "shape; brigade writes the document to the cache when it is true, and collects afresh on"
		+ "every call, inside a run or outside, a collector whose document carries false or no"
		+ "cache key"
		REF @TASK.B47
	DESC "outside a run the two files of a document not cached go under"
		+ "$XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/collect/<name>/, the layout of the run directory, never under"
		+ "the cache"
	DESC "the five built-ins declare true, through describe_collection"
	DESC "cache true requires declared cache inputs: a collector whose document declares cache true"
		+ "and for which no cache input is declared is refused naming it, where"
		+ "brigade/collecting/read_cache_input.py keys the five built-ins alone and would key any"
		+ "other collector on none, its entry never invalidated outside --refresh; carried by"
		+ "@TASK.B181"
		REF @TASK.B181
	REJECTED "a declaration file beside the executable, or an operation asked before the"
		+ "collection: a second thing every collector carries and a second read per call, where the"
		+ "document is already read and validated"
	REJECTED "a constant of the module for a built-in alone: a module and an executable would"
		+ "declare it in two ways, where the core tells no module plugin from an executable one"
	REJECTED "the files of a document not cached written under the cache directory and ignored by"
		+ "the next call: the user ruled that such a document is not put in the cache"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled that each collector declares whether its document is cached, false"
		+ "when it declares nothing, and left open how an executable declares it; this decision is"
		+ "the reading of that ruling by the session of the review round: the document is the one"
		+ "answer the contract already validates, and a declaration in it reads the same from a"
		+ "module and from an executable, as"
		+ "@DECISION.PluginsAreReachedByNameThroughOneResolverAndNeverImported requires"
		REF @DECISION.PluginsAreReachedByNameThroughOneResolverAndNeverImported
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-15 on review 5525912035 of pull request #136 of the"
		+ "brigade repository: « je pense que ça doit être géré par un boolean, car potentiellement"
		+ "tous les documents n'ont pas les mêmes besoins en terme de cache, certains peut être ne"
		+ "doivent pas être mis en cache? »; « Hors cache par défaut — Un collecteur n'est mis en"
		+ "cache que s'il le déclare : chaque intégré déclare cache = true. »"
		REF @TASK.B47
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-17 in the triage of the use-case map, answer \"C10: amend"
		+ "the cache decision\": DESC 4 added"
	SOURCE "use-case map of 2026-10-16, finding C10"

DECISION RunsPruneRemovesTheRunsBeyondTheBoundAndThoseSettledBeforeTheDay
	TITLE "brigade runs prune removes a finished or dead run that lies beyond the bound or was"
		+ "settled before the day of --before: the union of both"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the bound is --keep, else runs_kept of config.toml, its default when the file is absent;"
		+ "--before adds every run settled before midnight UTC of its day, whatever its rank"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B60"
		REF @TASK.B60
	REJECTED "--before in place of the bound: the call would leave runs/ above runs_kept until the"
		+ "next run removes the rest"
	REJECTED "the intersection, a run removed only when beyond the bound and before the day:"
		+ "--before would spare the old runs under the bound, where it removes them whatever their"
		+ "number"
	RATIONALE "a call of brigade runs prune bounds runs/ at once, whatever the day it is given, and"
		+ "--before reaches the old runs the bound would keep"
	SOURCE "pull request #134 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B60"
		REF @TASK.B60

DECISION WaveShowReadsThePullRequestOfATaskFromItsDeliveredByAtTheBranch
	TITLE "brigade wave show reads the pull request of a task from its DELIVERED_BY in the corpus"
		+ "at the wave's BRANCH, and from no ledger event"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the pull request column of wave show is the DELIVERED_BY of the TASK as the project's"
		+ "corpus holds it at BRANCH, through the tree cache of brigade corpus; a task without"
		+ "DELIVERED_BY shows none"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B11"
		REF @TASK.B11
	REJECTED "a pr field on task.state: the task declares the event with wave, task and state alone"
	REJECTED "the pr of the last pr.merged event of the task: it names only merged pull requests,"
		+ "and wave show already reads the corpus at BRANCH for the tasks and their TITLE"
	RATIONALE "a task's pull request promotes the task in the pull request itself, so the corpus at"
		+ "the integration branch carries DELIVERED_BY as soon as the pull request merges into it;"
		+ "one read serves the rows and their pull requests"
	SOURCE "pull request #137, the run of @TASK.B11 of 2026-10-15, the SPEC naming a pull request"
		+ "column and no source for it"
		REF @TASK.B11
	SOURCE "the user's ratification of 2026-10-15 in the review of pull request #137: DELIVERED_BY"
		+ "at BRANCH is the one source the corpus carries, with no call to the forge"

DECISION ProjectCommandsRunAsAnArgvWithoutAShell
	TITLE "every command brigade runs for a project or a study, PROJECT.SETUP, PROJECT.ACCEPTANCE"
		+ "and the command of a STUDY.COLLECTOR, runs through the runner as one argv split by"
		+ "shlex.split, never through sh -c"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a value of PROJECT.SETUP, PROJECT.ACCEPTANCE or of the shell: form of STUDY.COLLECTOR is"
		+ "one call: split with shlex.split into the argv the runner of"
		+ "@DECISION.OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa runs; a value shlex.split"
		+ "refuses is refused, naming it, before any command runs"
		REF @DECISION.OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa
	DESC "the lines of PROJECT.SETUP run in their order and stop at the first failure, in place of"
		+ "&&; each PROJECT.ACCEPTANCE line is one check run whatever the others returned"
	DESC "a command that needs a shell feature, a chain inside one line, a variable, a redirection,"
		+ "a pipe or a condition, is a script versioned by the project, called as one argv"
	DESC "a value of PROJECT.HEAVY, a suite left to the continuous integration that brigade never"
		+ "runs, is written in the same serialization of one argv, so that every project command"
		+ "has one form"
	DESC "the string field is the serialization of that argv until @TASK.B163 moves the project's"
		+ "commands to argv arrays in TOML versioned by the project"
		REF @TASK.B163
	DESC "it applies @DECISION.OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa without"
		+ "exception: no sh -c and no shell=True, whatever the field the command comes from"
		REF @DECISION.OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa
	DESC "the line of brigade/adapters/schedulers/data/crontab-line.tpl, run by cron through its"
		+ "own shell, is outside this decision; @TASK.B163 audits it"
		REF @TASK.B163
	DESC "binds @TASK.B12, @TASK.B48 and @TASK.B142"
		REF @TASK.B12
		REF @TASK.B48
		REF @TASK.B142
	REJECTED "a POSIX sh line run by /bin/sh -c, as an exception named in"
		+ "OneRunnerForEverySubprocessAndGatewaysForGitAndAwawa: quoting defects, and a second"
		+ "language inside the registry"
	REJECTED "declaring the commands in the project tree now, as TOML arrays or steps: a format"
		+ "imposed on every project before the recipe engine of M8 exists"
	RATIONALE "pull request #142 ran each PROJECT.SETUP line through sh -c and its review thread"
		+ "4286237837 asked which interpreter; pull request #143 ran the shell: form of a collector"
		+ "through sh -c; the user ruled that no command passes as a string, then to keep the plan"
		+ "and change nothing now: the defect is interpretation by a shell, not storage, so the"
		+ "field stays a string serializing one argv, a fixture that chained two commands with &&"
		+ "becomes two lines, and the home in the project tree waits for the engine of M8"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-15: « Dans tous les cas il est hors de question qu'on"
		+ "passe des commandes dans des chaines de caractère. Je veux qu'on fasse les choses"
		+ "proprement. »"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-16: « on va faire au plus simple, on colle au plan"
		+ "initial, on change rien pour l'instant, mais on enregistre une tâche en m8 pour vérifier"
		+ "deux choses: que l'on ne passe plus de commandes dans des strings, qu'il n'y a plus de"
		+ "chevauchement (commandes qui font la même chose par exemple), et prévoir un plan de"
		+ "remédiation si c'est pas réglé. »"
	SOURCE "the user's « ok » of 2026-10-16 on the session's recommendation: in #142 SETUP runs as"
		+ "an argv without a shell, split by shlex.split, the fixture in two lines; B142 SPEC 1"
		+ "runs argv; the shell: form leaves B48; the field stays a string that serializes an argv,"
		+ "the defect being interpretation by a shell, not storage, and the final home, TOML arrays"
		+ "versioned by the project, waits for the M8 engine; review thread 4286237837 of pull"
		+ "request #142"

DECISION TheTickGitignoresBrigadeWorktreesAloneAndTheProjectVersionsItsCollectorsAndRecipes
	TITLE "the tick adds .brigade/worktrees/ alone to a project's .gitignore; .brigade/collectors/"
		+ "and .brigade/recipes/ are versioned by the project"
	STATUS active
	DESC "under the default worktree root, the line the tick adds to the project's .gitignore is"
		+ ".brigade/worktrees/, never .brigade/"
	DESC ".brigade/collectors/ is the project's collectors directory of"
		+ "brigade/system/collector_places.py, where"
		+ "@DECISION.AStudyIsDeterministicCollectorsThenOneJudgingRun resolves collectors first,"
		+ "and .brigade/recipes/ the project's recipes directory of"
		+ "@DECISION.AKindOfWorkIsARecipeAnInstanceAnOrder: both are versioned with the project and"
		+ "ignored by nothing brigade writes"
		REF @DECISION.AStudyIsDeterministicCollectorsThenOneJudgingRun
		REF @DECISION.AKindOfWorkIsARecipeAnInstanceAnOrder
	DESC "binds @TASK.B12"
		REF @TASK.B12
	REJECTED "ignoring .brigade/ whole, as SPEC 5 of B12 read at its ratification: the project's"
		+ "collectors and recipes under it would never reach a commit"
	RATIONALE "the worktrees the tick cuts are disposable and the collectors and recipes of a"
		+ "project are its versioned files; one directory holds both, so the ignore line names the"
		+ "disposable part alone"
	SOURCE "the user's « ok » of 2026-10-16 on the session's recommendation: only"
		+ ".brigade/worktrees/ is gitignored"

DECISION TheUseCaseMapIsKeptAsSourcesToBeRedone
	TITLE "the use-case map is kept in artifact/use-cases/ with the briefs that redo it, and each"
		+ "Artifact of the repository has a subfolder of artifact/"
	STATUS active
	DESC "artifact/use-cases/ holds the page of the Artifact \"Brigade cas d'utilisation\", the"
		+ "data files it fetches and the briefs of the runs that produce them; redoing the map"
		+ "reruns those briefs and republishes the page, never edits the data by hand"
	DESC "the sources of the Blueprint move to artifact/blueprint/; a path of the corpus naming"
		+ "them names the new place"
		REF @DECISION.TheBlueprintIsADevelopmentArtefactRetiredByTheDashboard
	DESC "the page carries no automated test; it is checked by viewing it served locally, then"
		+ "published"
	REJECTED "the sources in the session's scratchpad only: the exercise could not be redone"
	REJECTED "artifact/use-cases/ beside the Blueprint's index.html and parts/ at the root of"
		+ "artifact/: two Artifacts sharing one folder"
	RATIONALE "the map is a snapshot of the project by use case, worth redoing as the plan moves;"
		+ "the briefs and the data shape are what a later session would otherwise rediscover"
	SOURCE "the user's words of 2026-10-16, « On pourra ranger les fichiers nécessaires à"
		+ "l'artefact dans un dossier du projet au cas où on a besoin de refaire cet exercice plus"
		+ "tard », and their answer « artifcat/use-cases/ and we move the blueprint's related files"
		+ "inside a blueprint subfolder »"

DECISION TheOutputStepOfAStudyRunWritesTheAnswerStudyAnswerRecorded
	TITLE "brigade study answer validates the answer and records it in the run directory; the"
		+ "output step of brigade study run writes it to the declared output"
	STATUS active
	DESC "study answer writes runs/<id>/answer.awawa; the judge step is done once that file exists,"
		+ "and the output step reads it, or renders the fields the CLI filled for a study with SLOT"
		+ "none, and writes it to the output"
	DESC "file:<path pattern>, {run} standing for the run, commits the Markdown on the branch"
		+ "brigade/study-<study>-<run>, created afresh in a worktree under the run directory, and"
		+ "force-pushes it, the branch being the run's alone, with a pull request where the project"
		+ "has a forge"
	DESC "issue opens a forge issue holding the Markdown; any other name but inbox is handed to"
		+ "brigade-output-<name> on PATH as a JSON document of schema_version, study, run and"
		+ "markdown on its stdin"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B48"
		REF @TASK.B48
	REJECTED "study answer writing the output itself: a failed push or issue would fall to the"
		+ "judging run to retry, where the output step parks the study and its next run resumes"
		+ "there without judging again"
	RATIONALE "the output is one step of the study run, as SPEC 3 of @TASK.B48 orders it, so a"
		+ "failed write is parked and resumed like any step, and one writer of the output serves"
		+ "the scan and the judged study alike"
		REF @TASK.B48
	SOURCE "pull request #143 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B48"
		REF @TASK.B48

DECISION TheInboxOutputOfAStudyIsRefusedUntilTheInboxHasAStore
	TITLE "brigade study new and brigade study run refuse the output inbox until task B22 gives the"
		+ "inbox a store"
	STATUS archived
	DESC "archived on 2026-10-24: @TASK.B22 gives the inbox its store and accepts the output inbox"
		+ "of a study, which records the answer as a signal"
	DESC "study new refuses OUTPUT inbox before it records the study, and study run refuses it"
		+ "before its run starts, for a study recorded earlier; each exits 1 naming the output and"
		+ "@TASK.B22"
		REF @TASK.B22
	DESC "brigade writes no inbox file; @TASK.B22 carries the inbox output of a study with the"
		+ "signals store"
		REF @TASK.B22
	DESC "binds @TASK.B48"
		REF @TASK.B48
	REJECTED "one Markdown file per run under $XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/inbox/, as the first delivery"
		+ "of #143 wrote it: the signals store of task B22 plans is JSONL with fingerprint, count,"
		+ "age and status, and would not read those files"
	CLOSES @OPEN_QUESTION.WhereTheInboxOutputOfAStudyIsStored
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-16 on pull request #143: « Refuser inbox d'ici B22 » — «"
		+ "study new et study run refusent la sortie `inbox` tant que B22 n'est pas livrée. On"
		+ "retire le code d'écriture des fichiers, et B22 portera cette sortie. »"
		REF @TASK.B48

DECISION ARunCarriesItsWaveAndItsTaskInRunJsonAndInEveryRunFinished
	TITLE "brigade run takes optional --wave and --task, the tick passes them, and run.json and"
		+ "every run.finished of the run carry them; brigade run stays generic"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade run takes --wave <wave>, the name of the wave, and --task <task>, both optional"
		+ "and independent; a run launched outside a wave carries wave null with the reason not"
		+ "launched by a wave, and a run launched for no task carries task null with the reason not"
		+ "launched for a task"
	DESC "the tick passes --wave and --task to every build run it launches"
	DESC "run.json and every run.finished of the run carry wave and task; the cost views and the"
		+ "wave report read them from run.finished"
	DESC "a run.json without the two keys is refused, naming the file and the key, its"
		+ "schema_version unchanged; brigade runs list lists such a run under skipped and brigade"
		+ "runs show fails on it; never upgraded"
	DESC "SPEC 1 of @TASK.B151, wave and task null on every run, becomes false once @TASK.B164"
