DECISION ARateLimitOfAnyRunPausesEveryRunningWaveUntilItsReset
	TITLE "a run.finished of any run on rate_limit pauses every running wave until its reset, and a"
		+ "pause in force binds the waves started during it"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a rate limit is in force from a run.finished on the error_class rate_limit, of any run of"
		+ "the machine, until the reset it names read from the instant of that run.finished, or 30"
		+ "minutes after it when reset is null, once no live run holds it"
	DESC "a running wave with no pause is paused on the quota while a running wave is paused on the"
		+ "quota with a resume_at not reached, with the latest such resume_at; otherwise while a"
		+ "rate limit is in force, with the resume_at SPEC 1 of @TASK.B19 sets"
		REF @TASK.B19
	DESC "a running task, or a task in fixing whose repair run was cut, moves to paused:quota when"
		+ "its last run.finished, keyed by its wave and its task, ends on rate_limit and no live"
		+ "run holds it; a run so cut spends no repair round, and after the reset it is launched"
		+ "again as @DECISION.QuotaPausesTheWaveAndResumesTheSameSession provides"
		REF @DECISION.QuotaPausesTheWaveAndResumesTheSameSession
	DESC "a wave started after forge_account.unavailable is paused on the forge account like the"
		+ "waves running then: only brigade wave resume lifts that pause"
	DESC "the pause of a task in fixing and the round it spares bind @TASK.B220; until it is"
		+ "delivered a task in fixing stays fixing and the tick launches a new repair run at each"
		+ "tick, one round each"
		REF @TASK.B220
	REJECTED "the build run of a running task of a running wave alone: the user ruled that any run"
		+ "on rate_limit pauses the waves, a study run or a run launched by hand included"
	REJECTED "every run.finished on rate_limit the ledger holds: a rate limit whose reset has"
		+ "passed, one recorded before the waves paused included, would pause every wave started"
		+ "later"
	REJECTED "the reset of a rate limit read from the tick's clock: the rate limit would stay in"
		+ "force at every tick and pause the waves again after each resume"
	REJECTED "a wave started during a quota pause left running: the user ruled that it is paused"
		+ "with the same resume_at, one client serving every project of the machine"
	REJECTED "a wave.started after forge_account.unavailable clearing the pause of that wave: the"
		+ "user ruled the clause out, the account being as unavailable as before"
	REJECTED "the last run.finished of the task whatever its state: a task awaiting its preflight"
		+ "or its verdict, or merged, would move back to paused:quota"
	REJECTED "a repair run cut by a rate limit counted as one round and launched again at the next"
		+ "tick, as the tick did until the ruling of 2026-10-29: on 2026-10-28 each tick launched"
		+ "on B211 a remediation that died in 1 to 7 steps on the 5-hour limit, each launch a"
		+ "round, until the task was parked past its rounds"
	RATIONALE "@TASK.B164 keys every run.finished by its wave and its task, so the run a rate limit"
		+ "stopped is found without reading run.json"
		REF @TASK.B164
	RATIONALE "on 2026-10-28 the runs 20261028T223554Z-9d1b1f and 20261028T224054Z-8eea2b of"
		+ "@TASK.B211 ended on « You've hit your 5-hour limit · resets 1:30am (Europe/Paris) », a"
		+ "message the adapter classified execution, and brigade/tick/build_snapshot.py _note_quota"
		+ "reads the rate limit of a running task alone, so no wave paused and the task in fixing"
		+ "spent a round at each tick; a run the quota cut did no repair, so it spends no round"
		REF @TASK.B211
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-29 in session, on the remediation runs of @TASK.B211 cut"
		+ "by the 5-hour limit on 2026-10-28, each launch counted as a round: « Ne compte aucun"
		+ "round »"
		REF @TASK.B211
	SOURCE "pull request #156 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B19, and the user's"
		+ "rulings of 2026-10-19 on its review: \"(1) B (2) B (3) B\""
		REF @TASK.B19

DECISION ACommandModuleIsNamedAfterItsCommandLineSoTheLineImportsItAlone
	TITLE "a command module is named after its command line, so brigade/cli.py imports the module"
		+ "of the line it runs alone and parses a help or a usage error again with every record"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a module of brigade/commands/ is named after the path of its command line, its words"
		+ "joined by _ and every - written _: runs_list for brigade runs list, adapter_launch_argv"
		+ "for brigade adapter launch-argv; a passthrough record is named after the module of its"
		+ "path, then _ and the tool it passes to, corpus_awawa;"
		+ "tests/guards/find_misnamed_command_modules.py proves it"
	DESC "brigade/select_command_modules.py picks, among the words of the arguments before --, the"
		+ "longest leading run that names a module, and with -- every module opening on that name"
		+ "and _; brigade/cli.py imports those alone and parses with a parser that raises where"
		+ "argparse would print, --version selecting none"
		REF @TASK.B191
	DESC "a help, a usage error, or arguments that name no module, are parsed again by the parser"
		+ "built from the records of every module, as before @TASK.B191: one parser prints the"
		+ "help, the usage errors and the order of the lines"
		REF @TASK.B191
	REJECTED "a hand-written table from command paths to modules: one more place to touch per"
		+ "command, REJECTED 7 of TheCodeIsOneFlatPackageWhoseSubpackagesFollowTheComponents"
	REJECTED "the records read from the sources with ast before any import: a second reader of the"
		+ "record, which the import already is"
	REJECTED "the help spotted by looking for -h or --help in the arguments: argparse takes an"
		+ "abbreviation, --he, and a usage error lists the sibling lines, so the full parser is"
		+ "needed wherever argparse prints"
	REJECTED "the parser built from the records of the whole group of the line: brigade runs list"
		+ "would import every runs module, and only a help or an error reads the siblings"
	RATIONALE "the parser needs the record of the line it runs alone, but its help and its usage"
		+ "errors read every record; parsing first with the one record and again with all when"
		+ "argparse would print keeps one parser for every message and pays the imports only where"
		+ "a person reads the output"
	SOURCE "pull request #160 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B191, which left the"
		+ "design to its implementer"
		REF @TASK.B191

DECISION AVerificationRunEndedWithoutAVerdictIsNotRelaunchedAtTheSameHead
	TITLE "the tick starts no second verification of a head whose review run ended without a"
		+ "verdict, unless that run ended on a rate limit"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a task in verifying gets a run of the slot review while no task.verdict is recorded at"
		+ "the head of its pull request, no live run holds its worktree, and no run.finished of the"
		+ "slot review for the task, other than with the error_class rate_limit, follows its last"
		+ "task.preflighted"
	DESC "a task in verifying whose pull request head is no longer the head of its last"
