		+ "its head, to the count of its failing check runs; that subject is the one the"
		+ "fingerprint names, through brigade/collecting/name_check_run_subject.py"
	DESC "the forge answers the check runs of the open pull requests and of the head of a branch"
		+ "through list_check_runs, and the steps of a job through read_job_steps, none for a link"
		+ "naming no job; check-runs declares cache false, as pr-list does"
	DESC "the tick plans CollectCheckRuns for each registered project whose STATUS is not paused"
		+ "and whose FORGE is github, and applies those actions once after its rounds through the"
		+ "executor of the rounds: a failure is a tick.action_failed naming the project, counted in"
		+ "actions_failed"
