DECISION TheTriageGroupsSignalsByKeyAndAPatternCitesASignalByOpeningAnEvidenceOnItsFingerprint
	TITLE "the built-in triage groups the new signals by rule cited, file and check name, and a"
		+ "PATTERN cites a signal by an EVIDENCE that is its fingerprint or opens on it followed by"
		+ "a space"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a family is the signals sharing one key, kept from two signals on: a @RULE.<name> cited"
		+ "in a string of the evidence, the evidence path, the evidence name of a signal of kind"
		+ "check_run; a signal shares several families when it holds several keys, and a signal in"
		+ "none is a family of one"
	DESC "the built-in triage is a study of the code, EVERY 24h; a STUDY of the operational corpus"
		+ "named triage replaces it, to pause it or change its schedule"
	DESC "an answer of type PATTERN is linted beside the patterns.awawa of the operational corpus,"
		+ "and refused when a PATTERN of the answer is not new, names no ACTION, holds no EVIDENCE"
		+ "or holds an EVIDENCE opening on no fingerprint inbox-families collected; the patterns"
		+ "the operational corpus already holds are linted, never checked"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B25"
		REF @TASK.B25
	REJECTED "an EVIDENCE that contains the fingerprint anywhere: rt:101 would cite rt:1012, and a"
		+ "check name holding a space forbids reading the first word alone"
	REJECTED "families joined transitively into one group: one shared file would merge two"
		+ "unrelated rules into one problem"
	REJECTED "the built-in triage written into the operational corpus by brigade init: init"
		+ "upgrades no installed corpus, so the machines already initialised would never run it"
	REJECTED "the check run on the patterns held beside the answer: a held pattern is ratified or"
		+ "cites signals inbox-families no longer collects, so every triage after the first would"
		+ "be refused"
	RATIONALE "the collector must recognise the signals a PATTERN already cites, so that none is"
		+ "proposed twice, and the check of the answer is the same rule read from the other side"
	SOURCE "pull request 211, which delivers @TASK.B25"
		REF @TASK.B25

DECISION RatificationNamesItsEntitiesAfterThePatternAndTheClosedWaveDeliversThePattern
	TITLE "brigade inbox ratify names the CONSTRAINT and the ORDER after their PATTERN, and the"
		+ "close of the wave that delivers the request of a pattern delivers the PATTERN and its"
		+ "CONSTRAINT"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a CONSTRAINT and an ORDER a ratification records bear the name of their PATTERN"
	DESC "brigade inbox ratify takes --kind for a pattern of ACTION constraint, KIND being required"
		+ "on a CONSTRAINT and absent from a PATTERN, and refuses a pattern of ACTION dismiss,"
		+ "naming brigade inbox dismiss"
	DESC "brigade inbox dismiss names a PATTERN when the operational corpus defines one by that"
		+ "name, a signal otherwise"
	DESC "a wave report row PATTERN_TASK reads <task> from @PATTERN.<name> with @CONSTRAINT.<name>:"
		+ "<the TITLE of the pattern>, for each task whose MILESTONE is that of a REQUEST FROM a"
		+ "pattern"
	DESC "the tick delivers at wave.closed: every PATTERN a REQUEST of the project comes FROM,"
		+ "whose MILESTONE a task of the closed wave carries, goes delivered with each CONSTRAINT"
		+ "FROM it, and constraint.delivered is appended once per constraint"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B26"
		REF @TASK.B26
	REJECTED "a KIND guessed from the pattern: the triage answer carries no KIND, and a wrong guess"
		+ "would deliver the wrong kind of artefact"
	REJECTED "delivery when the task pull requests merge into the integration branch: the wave is"
		+ "delivered once its integration pull request reaches the main branch, which the tick"
		+ "reads as wave.closed"
	RATIONALE "the request of a pattern is planned into one MILESTONE, so the milestones the tasks"
		+ "of a closed wave carry are what links the wave back to the patterns it delivers"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-24 in the refinement of B23 to B26, and the build run of"
		+ "@TASK.B26"
		REF @TASK.B26

