DECISION ATaskBranchIsCutRebasedAndCheckedAgainstTheIntegrationBranchOfTheForge
	TITLE "on a project of FORGE github, a task branch is cut from, rebased onto and checked"
		+ "against origin/<integration> fetched at its launch; a project of FORGE none keeps its"
		+ "local integration branch"
	STATUS active
	DESC "binds @TASK.B210"
		REF @TASK.B210
	REJECTED "the local integration branch, as prepare_task_worktree.py cuts and checks it before"
		+ "B210: the tick merges task pull requests with gh pr merge on GitHub, so the local branch"
		+ "lags behind the merges and a new task branch starts from a stale base"
	REJECTED "the rebase alone on origin, the cut and the check kept local: two references for one"
		+ "branch, the check failing whenever they differ"
	RATIONALE "the integration branch moves on the forge, where the task pull requests merge and"
		+ "where the wave report is pushed; one reference read after a fetch gives every launch the"
		+ "same base, as @DECISION.AGithubProjectPlansAndStartsItsWavesFromTheMainBranchOfTheForge"
		+ "does for MAIN"
		REF @DECISION.AGithubProjectPlansAndStartsItsWavesFromTheMainBranchOfTheForge
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-28 in the refinement of @TASK.B210,"
		+ "\"origin/<integration>\" then \"Tout sur origin (Recommandé)\""
		REF @TASK.B210

DECISION ARebaseRunOfATaskWithoutAPullRequestEndsDoneAndTheTickLaunchesItsBuild
	TITLE "a rebase run launched at the launch of a task with no pull request takes the arguments"
		+ "task and base, reads its task from the branch of the worktree, pushes nothing, and the"
		+ "next tick launches the build run once that run ended done"
	STATUS active
	DESC "binds @TASK.B210"
		REF @TASK.B210
	DESC "brigade rebase context without a pull request reads the task and its wave from the branch"
		+ "task/<slug>/<task> of the worktree, as brigade task context does"
	DESC "the task stays running while that run lives; a running task with no pull request whose"
		+ "last run is a rebase run ended done is launched again, not parked as a dead run"
	DESC "brigade wave requeue compares the entity of the task on both branches only when the main"
		+ "branch defines it"
	REJECTED "a state of its own for a task under a rebase run: running already parks the task on"
		+ "the question of a run that ended blocked, and a new state would add a case to every"
		+ "reader of the states"
	REJECTED "a push of the rebased branch by the rebase run: a branch with no pull request is"
		+ "pushed by the build run when it opens one"
	RATIONALE "@TASK.B210 leaves open how a run of the rebase slot works on a task that has no pull"
		+ "request, which brigade rebase context and the procedure rebase-on-base named by its"
		+ "number"
		REF @TASK.B210
	SOURCE "the build run of @TASK.B210 on 2026-10-28"
		REF @TASK.B210

