DECISION TheTickReadsTheWavesOfAMilestoneAtItsBranchAndACancelledWaveCountsNeither
	TITLE "the tick reads the waves of a milestone from the ledger and the tasks at the branch of"
		+ "the milestone: a closed wave whose tasks name the milestone there is merged, an open"
		+ "wave is one the tick follows on that branch, and a cancelled wave counts neither"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a closed wave belongs to a milestone when one of its tasks names that MILESTONE in the"
		+ "corpus at the branch of the milestone; its pull request is the pr of its wave.closed"
	DESC "an open wave belongs to a milestone when the branch of its milestone, read as the tick"
		+ "reads it to open the pull request of the wave, is the branch of the milestone, or when"
		+ "one of its tasks names that MILESTONE in the corpus at the branch of the milestone: the"
		+ "ledger holds it open even when its branch is missing or its reading failed"
	DESC "a cancelled wave is neither closed nor open: it neither opens nor holds back the pull"
		+ "request of its milestone, and a task it left todo at the branch of the milestone holds"
		+ "it back as SPEC 1 of @TASK.B215 sets"
		REF @TASK.B215
	DESC "the tree of the branch of a milestone is read until milestone.pr_opened only; from then"
		+ "on the tick reads the pull request of the branch alone"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B215"
		REF @TASK.B215
	REJECTED "a cancelled wave counted as a wave not closed: nothing closes a cancelled wave, so"
		+ "its milestone would never open its pull request"
	REJECTED "the tree of the branch of a milestone read at every tick until milestone.closed: on a"
		+ "forge that deletes the head branch of a merged pull request the fetch fails, and"
		+ "milestone.closed is never appended"
	RATIONALE "SPEC 1 of @TASK.B215 asks every wave of the milestone closed and none open, and"
		+ "names no cancelled wave; summarize_waves ends a wave on wave.closed or wave.cancelled"
		REF @TASK.B215
	SOURCE "the build run of @TASK.B215, 2026-10-30"
		REF @TASK.B215

DECISION TheCheckRepairBriefNamesTheCoverageRemedyOnAFailingCheckWhoseNameHoldsCoverage
	TITLE "the brief of a check repair tells the coverage check by its name holding coverage, in"
		+ "any case, and carries every preflight failure other than checks, ancestry included"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a failing check whose name holds coverage, compared after casefold, is the coverage check"
		+ "of the brief: its failure adds the remedy of an uncovered line"
	DESC "the other findings of the brief are every failure of the preflight of the same head but"
		+ "checks, whose logs the brief already carries; ancestry is among them"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B218"
		REF @TASK.B218
	REJECTED "a key of config.toml or a field of PROJECT naming the coverage check: the forge names"
		+ "a check after its job, and every coverage job brigade drives so far holds the word"
	REJECTED "the findings of the changes requested alone, ancestry left out as _describe_request"
		+ "does: SPEC 1 of the task asks for every other finding of the preflight"
	RATIONALE "the check of brigade is Coverage of the unit tests by coverage.py; a brief that"
		+ "names the remedy on a check that is not one costs a paragraph, a brief that misses it"
		+ "costs a verdict, as the coverage repair of @TASK.B28 did"
		REF @TASK.B28
	SOURCE "the build run of @TASK.B218 of 2026-10-29, which left this ruling open"
		REF @TASK.B218

DECISION ARequeueReadsThePullRequestOfItsTaskFromTheLedgerAndSetsAsideTheVerificationRecordedBeforeIt
	TITLE "brigade wave requeue finds the pull request of a parked task in the ledger, and the tick"
		+ "reads the preflight and the verdict of a task from the events recorded after its last"
		+ "requeue, so that an unchanged head is preflighted and verified again"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a parked task has an open pull request for brigade wave requeue when the ledger holds a"
		+ "task.pr_opened of the task in its wave; a pull request closed since is parked again by"
		+ "the next tick, on the reason pull request closed"
	DESC "the task.state brigade wave requeue records carries the reason brigade wave requeue; the"
		+ "tick reads the preflighted head, the preflight failures, the verdict and the reviewed"
		+ "head of a task from the events recorded after the last task.state of that reason"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B217"
		REF @TASK.B217
	REJECTED "the forge asked by brigade wave requeue whether the pull request is open: the requeue"
		+ "would need the forge account of a slot for a fact the next tick reads anyway, and a"
		+ "closed pull request is parked again by that tick"
	REJECTED "the preflight and the verdict kept across a requeue: an unchanged head is not"
		+ "preflighted again, the verdict recorded on it is applied again without a verification,"
		+ "and the remediation receives no fresh preflight"
	RATIONALE "the count of the rounds and the mark of the requeue are read from the ledger alone,"
		+ "as @DECISION.TheTickIsAPurePlannerAndAnExecutorThatRecordsEveryAction asks"
		REF @DECISION.TheTickIsAPurePlannerAndAnExecutorThatRecordsEveryAction
	SOURCE "pull request #251 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B217"
		REF @TASK.B217

DECISION ARunCutByARateLimitSpendsNoRoundOnceResumedAndItsResumeRestoresTheStateHeldBeforeThePause
	TITLE "a run of which a segment ended on rate_limit spends no round, resumed or not, the"
		+ "task.state its resume records spends none, and the resume restores the state the task"
		+ "held before paused:quota"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the task.state fixing recorded at the launch of a run counts no round when a run.finished"
		+ "of that run, of any segment, ends on rate_limit, whether the run resumed after the reset"
		+ "ends done or not"
	DESC "the task.state fixing recorded by the resume of a task, the one following its"
		+ "paused:quota, counts no round"
	DESC "the resume of a task paused on the quota records the last task.state the task held before"
		+ "paused:quota: fixing for a repair run, running for a build run"
	DESC "the tick plans no action on the pull request of a task whose rate limit it notes, so that"
		+ "no repair is launched in the tick that pauses the task"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B220"
		REF @TASK.B220
	REJECTED "the launch of a cut run counted once its resumed segment ends done: the user ruled «"
		+ "Ne compte aucun round » for a run cut by a rate limit, and SPEC 4 of TASK B220 asks the"
		+ "rounds of the task unchanged after the resume"
	REJECTED "the state of the resume read from the slot of the run: a check repair runs in the"
		+ "build slot while its task is in fixing"
	REJECTED "every resume recording running, as the tick did: a task in fixing resumed into"
		+ "running would be recorded pr_open by the next tick, its repair abandoned"
	SOURCE "the delivery of @TASK.B220, on the user's ruling of 2026-10-29 « Ne compte aucun round"
		+ "»"
		REF @TASK.B220

DECISION TheAwawaDocumentPluginRendersAFileHoldingItsSchemaOnlyOnceLintAcceptsIt
	TITLE "the awawa document plugin renders a file that holds its schema only once awawa lint"
		+ "--strict accepts it, and a file it refuses as its raw text with entities null"
	STATUS active
	DESC "render_document of the awawa plugin runs awawa lint --strict on a file holding a SCHEMA"
		+ "entity, the progress of a run, and answers the text of the file whole with entities null"
		+ "when lint refuses it"
	DESC "a file whose schema lives outside it, the answer of a study, is rendered from its"
		+ "entities without that lint: the file alone is no corpus lint can accept, and the study"
		+ "validated it against its schema before"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B182"
		REF @TASK.B182
	REJECTED "the lint applied to every file the plugin renders: the answer of a study holds no"
		+ "schema and would always render as its raw text"
	REJECTED "a conformity operation added to the document kind for the progress alone: a second"
		+ "operation answering what the rendering already decides"
	RATIONALE "SPEC 4 of @TASK.B182 prints a progress.awawa caught in the middle of a write as its"
		+ "raw text and exits 0; the plugin decides it, so brigade runs show never names one form"
		+ "of the progress"
		REF @TASK.B182
	SOURCE "pull request #236 of the brigade repository, delivering @TASK.B182"
		REF @TASK.B182

DECISION ADashboardRouteTellsAnUnknownIdByItsListingCommand
	TITLE "a route of the dashboard that names an id or a project answers 404 when the listing"
		+ "command does not list it, takes the ref of brigade corpus from its query, and serves its"
		+ "fragment under /views/"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a route whose command exits non-zero runs the listing command of what it names, brigade"
		+ "wave list --json for a wave and brigade project list --json for a project, and answers"
		+ "404 when the id is absent from it, 500 when it is listed or the listing fails"
	DESC "/api/corpus/<project> passes its query parameter ref as --ref=<ref>; without it the"
		+ "command runs without --ref and its usage error answers 500"
	DESC "an id or a project starting with - is no id: the route answers 404 and runs nothing, so"
		+ "no path segment reaches the command line as an option"
	DESC "/views/<route> renders as an HTML fragment the document /api/<route> serves, under the"
		+ "same status; a view without a renderer of its own nests the fields of the document"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B27"
		REF @TASK.B27
	REJECTED "telling 404 from the standard error of the command: its messages are text, not a"
		+ "contract of the command line"
	REJECTED "the -- separator before the id: argparse treats it unevenly across the Python"
		+ "versions brigade supports, and brigade corpus reads -- as the start of awawa's arguments"
	RATIONALE "brigade corpus requires --ref or --worktree, which the route of @TASK.B27 does not"
		+ "name; @TASK.B30 reads the corpus through /api/corpus/<project> at a ref it selects"
		REF @TASK.B30
		REF @TASK.B27
	SOURCE "the build run of @TASK.B27 of 2026-10-28"
		REF @TASK.B27

DECISION TheDashboardAcceptsOnlyItsLoopbackHostAndATokenInAHeader
	TITLE "the dashboard accepts the Host 127.0.0.1:<port> alone, and a POST carries the token of"
		+ "the page in the header X-Brigade-Token"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the Host header is compared to 127.0.0.1:<port> exactly: localhost and every other name"
		+ "answer 400"
	DESC "the page holds the token in <meta name=\"brigade-token\">; a POST carries it in the"
		+ "header X-Brigade-Token, compared in constant time, with the Origin"
		+ "http://127.0.0.1:<port>"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B27"
		REF @TASK.B27
	REJECTED "accepting localhost: the server prints and binds 127.0.0.1, the origin of its page is"
		+ "that address, and a second accepted name widens what a rebound name can reach"
	REJECTED "the token in a cookie: a cookie is sent by every page that reaches the port, the"
		+ "header only by a script of the page"
	SOURCE "the build run of @TASK.B27 of 2026-10-28"
		REF @TASK.B27

DECISION TheInboxViewRendersTheFamiliesAndPatternsOfInboxListAndPostsItsActionsUnderApiInbox
	TITLE "brigade inbox list --json carries the families of the triage and the proposed patterns,"
		+ "the Inbox view renders them, and its actions are POSTs to /api/inbox/ratify/<pattern>"
		+ "and /api/inbox/dismiss/<id>"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade inbox list --json carries families, each with by, key and the ids of its signals,"
		+ "grouped among the signals it lists by brigade/inbox/group_signals.py, the grouping the"
		+ "built-in triage collects"
	DESC "a pattern of the document carries its name, its ACTION or null, and the ids of the"
		+ "signals of the inbox an EVIDENCE of it cites"
	DESC "POST /api/inbox/ratify/<pattern>?kind=<kind> runs brigade inbox ratify --kind=<kind>, the"
		+ "kind optional, and POST /api/inbox/dismiss/<id> runs brigade inbox dismiss; when the"
		+ "command fails, an id brigade inbox list does not name, among its patterns for ratify,"
		+ "its patterns and signals for dismiss, answers 404"
	DESC "a pattern of ACTION constraint shows one ratify button per KIND of CONSTRAINT, any other"
		+ "pattern one ratify button"
	DESC "binds @TASK.B29"
		REF @TASK.B29
	REJECTED "the view grouping the signals itself: the dashboard reads the command line, never the"
		+ "package, so the grouping stays in the command a port carries over"
	REJECTED "the evidence of each signal in brigade inbox list --json for the view to group: the"
		+ "grouping would be written twice, in the collector and in the view"
	REJECTED "one ratify button for a pattern of ACTION constraint: brigade inbox ratify refuses it"
		+ "without --kind"
	SOURCE "the build run of @TASK.B29 of 2026-10-28"
		REF @TASK.B29

DECISION BrigadeReportsListsTheWaveReportsAndStudyAnswersTheOperationalCorpusKeeps
	TITLE "brigade reports reads the REPORT and ANSWER entities of the operational corpus through"
		+ "the awawa document plugin; the outputs of an order join it with the engine that writes"
		+ "them"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a wave report is a REPORT entity of reports.awawa, kind wave-report, its project its"
		+ "PROJECT field; a study answer is an ANSWER entity of answers.awawa, kind study-answer,"
		+ "its project that of the STUDY it answers; the id is the name of the entity"
	DESC "an answer a study hands to a file, an issue, the inbox or an output on PATH is read where"
		+ "it was handed: brigade reports lists what the operational corpus keeps"
	DESC "no order output exists when @TASK.B31 is delivered: the engine of @TASK.B51 is a draft,"
		+ "and where it keeps the answer of a judge step is its to settle; it adds the kind of its"
		+ "outputs to brigade reports"
